+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use a VA loan on a condo in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only in a condo community the VA has approved. Horry County has about 175 on the VA's list, but just 2 of the 29 oceanfront resort buildings in our directory are among them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to live in the home with a VA loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You certify that you intend to move in, and most lenders want you in the home within 60 days. A beach house you visit or a home you rent out does not count."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do 100 percent disabled veterans pay property tax in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not on the home they live in, once the VA rates them 100 percent permanently and totally disabled from their service. It covers the home, up to 5 acres and up to two cars. You apply to the SC Department of Revenue after the county grants the 4 percent rate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pay the VA funding fee if I have a disability rating?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, if you receive VA compensation for a service-connected disability, or are eligible for it but receive retirement or active-duty pay instead."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use a VA loan more than once?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Once you have sold the home and paid off the VA loan, the VA can restore your entitlement when you ask. With a VA loan still open on another home, you may have entitlement left for a second one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What interest rate will I get on a VA loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The lender quotes your rate. We do not quote rates. We can introduce you to our preferred lender, or you can use any lender you like."}}]}</script>
