/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">A house you will live in</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="yes">Yes</i></span><span class="d">The seller must agree to a VA offer, and the house must pass the VA appraisal.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span class="k">A townhouse</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="yes">Usually</i></span><span class="d">If the community was set up as a condo, it must be on the VA's condo list, like any condo.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8.5 18.5V3.5l8 3.6-8 3.6M3.5 19c0-1.4 3.8-2.5 8.5-2.5s8.5 1.1 8.5 2.5-3.8 2.5-8.5 2.5-8.5-1.1-8.5-2.5z"/><circle cx="16" cy="15.2" r="1.2"/></svg></span><span class="k">A condo in a villa, golf or townhome community</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="maybe">Often</i></span><span class="d">The condo community must be on the VA's list. We look it up before you tour.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span class="k">A condo in an oceanfront resort tower</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="no">Rarely</i></span><span class="d">Only 2 of the 29 oceanfront resort buildings we track are on the VA's list.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">A beach second home or a rental</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="no">No</i></span><span class="d">A VA loan is only for the home you live in.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 20.5v-1a5 5 0 0 1 5-5h2a5 5 0 0 1 5 5v1M16 14.5h1a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="7" r="3.2"/><circle cx="17" cy="8.8" r="2.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">A house with 2 to 4 units</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="yes">Yes</i></span><span class="d">You must live in one of the units. The others can be rented.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The chart shows how often each kind of home for sale is marked as taking VA. Houses and townhouses are close to half. Condos fall to 9 in 100, and to 3 in 100 in oceanfront buildings.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes for sale marked as taking a VA loan, out of every 100"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes for sale marked as taking a VA loan, out of every 100</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind of home, how many for sale</span><span role="columnheader">marked VA</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">3,702 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.52" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">52 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Townhouses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">364 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.46" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">46 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">2,827 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.09" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">9 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos with a rental program</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">1,384 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.04" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos in an oceanfront building</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">1,088 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.03" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">3 in 100</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Chapter3's count of homes for sale on the Coastal Carolinas MLS, in aggregate, from the financing the listing says the seller will consider. A listing without the mark can still take VA. A condo in a building with a rental program, or in an oceanfront building, is also counted in all condos.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="va-approved-condos"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="VA-approved condos">Which condos in Myrtle Beach are VA-approved?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://lgy.va.gov/lgyhub/condo-report" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA's condo list</a> holds about 175 condo communities in Horry County. That is about 20 times as many as HUD's list for FHA loans, which holds 9. A VA loan on a condo needs a community on the VA's list.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The oceanfront is the exception. Of the 29 oceanfront resort buildings in our <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condo building directory</a>, 2 have an accepted VA record: Beach Cove Resort and the Renaissance Tower at Myrtle Beach Resort. None of the other 27 does.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:760px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px" width="1200" height="675" alt="A row of oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach with stacked balconies and pools behind the dunes, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, the kind of building that is rarely on the VA's list.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One community on both lists is Seagate Village, an 800-unit condo community of single and duplex homes on Mallard Lake Drive in Myrtle Beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What if your building needs VA approval?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A lender or the condo's sponsor can ask the VA to review it, with the condo's documents. Over the past year, the VA finished 27 reviews of Horry County condo projects: it accepted 22 and rejected 5.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We look up every condo on the VA's list before you write an offer. Our guide to <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condos most lenders will not lend on</a> covers the other loan rules a condo building can fail.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is your building on the VA's list?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building's name. We look it up on the VA's list and send you the condos for sale in VA-approved communities.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about a building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="sellers"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Sellers who take VA">Do sellers in Myrtle Beach accept VA offers?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most do inland, fewer at the beach. About 2 in 3 houses for sale in Conway and Longs are marked as taking VA, about half in Myrtle Beach, and about 3 in 10 in North Myrtle Beach.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses for sale marked as taking a VA loan, by town"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses for sale marked as taking a VA loan, by town</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town, houses for sale</span><span role="columnheader">share marked VA</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">673 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.67" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">67%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Longs</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">343 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.67" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">67%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Aynor</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">44 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.61" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">61%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">153 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.6" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">60%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">189 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.56" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">56%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">1,035 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">50%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">203 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.41" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">41%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">82 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.37" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">37%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">254 houses for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.28" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">28%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Towns are mailing addresses, so Myrtle Beach includes Carolina Forest and Socastee, and Conway includes country land outside the city.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By price, VA is most common on houses priced $250,000 to $300,000, where about 2 in 3 take it. At $1 million and up, about 1 in 4 do. The middle house marked VA is priced between $350,000 and $400,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">New houses take VA more often than older ones: about 7 in 10 new houses for sale are marked VA. In our experience, most builders here also offer incentives to buyers with FHA, VA and conventional loans. Our <a href="/buyers/new-construction/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">new construction guide</a> covers buying from a builder.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood zones and assumable loans</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 10 houses for sale listed as in a flood zone are marked VA. In a high-risk flood zone, a VA loan requires flood insurance for the life of the loan. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance guide</a> gives what it costs.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A buyer can also take over a seller's VA loan, called an assumable loan. Only 18 homes for sale on the Grand Strand are listed with an assumable loan of any kind, so we ask the seller's agent about the loan on each home you like.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Houses for sale whose sellers take VA</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the towns you like and your price range. We send the houses for sale there that are marked as taking a VA loan.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get the VA homes list</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="second-homes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Second homes and rentals">Can you buy a beach house or a rental with a VA loan?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not as a second home or a pure rental. A VA purchase loan is for the home you will live in, and you certify that you intend to move in. Most lenders require you to move in within 60 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you are on active duty and cannot live there because of it, your spouse can meet the rule.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You can rent part of what you buy. A VA loan can buy a house with up to 4 units if you live in one of them. You can also use the benefit again after you sell.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience, a house with a tenant on a long lease is hard to buy with a VA loan, because you must be able to move in. We ask about the lease before you make an offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="property-tax"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Property tax exemption">Do disabled veterans pay property tax in South Carolina?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not on their home, if the VA rates them permanently and totally disabled from a service-connected disability. The exemption covers the home they own and live in, alone or with a spouse, with up to 5 acres, and up to two cars.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The savings depend on where the home is. Conway's city tax is the highest, so a veteran there saves the most.</p><figure style="margin:1.2rem 0 1rem;max-width:620px"><table class="c3-va-tbl"><caption>Property tax a year a fully exempt veteran does not pay, on a home the county values at $400,000</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where the home is</th><th scope="col">Tax saved a year</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Conway</th><td>$2,610</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">North Myrtle Beach</th><td>$1,790</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Surfside Beach</th><td>$1,680</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">City of Myrtle Beach</th><td>$1,620</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Murrells Inlet or Garden City<small>Horry County side</small></th><td>$1,570</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Outside the cities<small>Carolina Forest, Socastee, Little River</small></th><td>$1,470</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin-top:.6rem">Chapter3's figures from the county's tax rates for a home you live in, worked out the same way as our property tax calculator. The county taxes its own value of the home, not the price you paid. Small special district taxes and the county's stormwater fee are left out.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A rating below permanent and total does not qualify. A surviving spouse who has not remarried and lives in the home keeps the exemption, and can move it to a later home. Every town's tax rate is in our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a>.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How to apply, in order</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The exemption is not automatic. The order matters, and the SC Department of Revenue grants it, not the county auditor. We walk you through these four steps after closing.</p><ol class="c3-va-steps"><li><strong>Get the 4 percent rate on your home.</strong>After closing, you apply to the Horry County Assessor for the 4 percent rate, the lower tax rate for the home you live in. The SC Department of Revenue will not grant the exemption until the county has.</li><li><strong>Get the disability certificate.</strong>It comes from the VA or from the county's veterans affairs office. A VA rating letter alone is not enough. <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/veterans-affairs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Veterans Affairs</a> is at 1949 Industrial Park Road in Conway, and its phone is (843) 915-5480.</li><li><strong>Apply to the SC Department of Revenue.</strong>Apply online in <a href="https://mydorway.dor.sc.gov/?link=PT401I" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MyDORWAY</a>, or on Form PT-401-I. Send the recorded deed, the county's 4 percent approval and the certificate.</li><li><strong>Claim the whole year.</strong>A newly rated veteran can claim the exemption for the whole year the disability began, if they owned the home that year; if they bought it later, from the year they bought it. A late filer can go back up to two prior tax years if the taxes were paid on time.</li></ol><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Rated below 100 percent?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At 65, with a year in South Carolina, the Homestead Exemption takes the first $50,000 of your home's value off the bill; for 2026 only, owners who already qualified in 2025 get $75,000. It also applies if a state or federal agency has classified you totally and permanently disabled. You apply to the county auditor by July 15.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="appraisal"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The VA appraisal">What does the VA appraisal check?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two things: that the home is worth what you agreed to pay, and that it meets the VA's minimum property requirements. The VA orders the appraisal.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The VA loan cannot be more than the appraised value or the price, whichever is lower. The VA's own example: on a home under contract for $400,000 that appraises at $375,000, the loan is capped at $375,000. You then pay the gap in cash, the seller lowers the price, or the deal ends.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Older homes get one extra look. In a home built before 1978, the VA presumes lead paint, and any peeling or damaged paint must be fixed before the loan closes. Homes that old are far less common here than in the country as a whole.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes built before 1980, out of every 100"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes built before 1980, out of every 100</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where</span><span role="columnheader">built before 1980</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Horry County</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.139" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">South Carolina</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.319" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">32 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">United States</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.481" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">48 in 100</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>U.S. Census Bureau, American Community Survey, one-year estimates for 2024, all homes.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer on a home built before 1978, we look for peeling paint, so you can ask the seller to fix it in the contract.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="closing"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Funding fee and closing costs">What does a VA buyer pay at closing?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Unless you are exempt, you pay a one-time <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA funding fee</a>. You can add it to the loan or pay it at closing. On a purchase it is the only cost you can add to the loan.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who pays no funding fee</h3><ul class="c3-va-cards" role="list" aria-label="Who pays no VA funding fee"><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>You receive VA disability compensation</strong>Or you are eligible for it but receive retirement or active-duty pay instead.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>You have a rating before closing</strong>A service member with a proposed or memorandum rating dated before the closing.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>You are a surviving spouse on DIC</strong>Dependency and Indemnity Compensation, as the surviving spouse of a veteran.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>You are on active duty with a Purple Heart</strong>You show the lender proof of it on or before the closing date.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the VA later awards you disability compensation that starts before your closing date, you can ask for the funding fee back.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the seller can pay</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A seller can pay all of your closing costs, and the VA does not limit that. Other help from the seller, such as paying your funding fee or paying off a debt, is capped at 4 percent of the home's reasonable value.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Who pays the commission, the loan origination fee, the VA appraisal fee and title insurance is up to you and the seller. We write the request into your offer. Our <a href="/buyers/closing-costs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">closing cost guide</a> lists each cost at closing in South Carolina.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="va-clinic"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The VA clinic">Where is the VA clinic in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Myrtle Beach VA Clinic is at 1800 Airpark Drive. It opened in 2021 for primary care, mental health and specialty care, and replaced two older clinics in town.</p><figure style="margin:1.4rem 0 .4rem;max-width:560px"><div class="c3-va-map"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic" viewBox="0 0 360 432" width="360" height="432" role="img" aria-label="Map of the Grand Strand with the Myrtle Beach VA Clinic and the drive to it from each town: Socastee about 10 minutes, Myrtle Beach about 12 minutes, Surfside Beach about 14 minutes, Carolina Forest about 20 minutes, Murrells Inlet about 20 minutes, Conway about 25 minutes, North Myrtle Beach about 35 minutes, Little River about 45 minutes, Loris about 55 minutes." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec;border:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.15)"><style>#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic text{font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#f7f3ec;stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .h{font:500 17px 'Fraunces',Georgia,serif}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .l{font-size:14px;font-weight:500}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .m{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;fill:#91592b}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .t{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;fill:#5c6b78}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .T{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;fill:#3b4450}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .o{font:italic 400 15px 'Fraunces',Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:.06em;fill:#3f6275;stroke:#c9dde6}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .p{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;fill:#4a6640}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .f{font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .r{font-size:11px;font-weight:500;stroke:none;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .q{font-size:8px;lett