stination=33.677414,-78.945299" title="Directions to Myrtle Beach VA Clinic in Google Maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--brass);text-underline-offset:3px"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align:-3px;margin-right:.35rem"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg>Get directions</a></p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The clinic is part of the Ralph H. Johnson VA health care system. From the clinic, the nearest VA medical center is the Ralph H. Johnson VA Medical Center in Charleston, about 2 hours 10 minutes away without traffic. From Loris, Little River and North Myrtle Beach, the Fayetteville VA Medical Center in North Carolina is a shorter drive.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The veteran community here</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 30,000 veterans live in Horry County, about 9 in 100 adults, against 6 in 100 nationally. The Myrtle Beach Air Force Base closed in 1993. Warbird Park keeps its history, with a Wall of Service that lists people who served at the base.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:760px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Military jets in camouflage paint on display on a round plaza with small plaques, under tall pines at Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/res/482_high.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Carol M. Highsmith. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Carol M. Highsmith</a></span></div><figcaption>Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach keeps the history of the Myrtle Beach Air Force Base.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina does not tax military retirement pay, and a surviving spouse gets the same deduction. Our <a href="/buyers/retirees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide for retirees</a> covers the rest of the state's taxes on retirement income.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="who-qualifies"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who qualifies">Who qualifies for a VA loan, and how much can you borrow?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You need a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) from the VA. These are the <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">service minimums</a> for service from the Gulf War to today:</p><ul class="c3-va-cards" role="list" aria-label="VA loan service minimums"><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Serving now</strong>90 continuous days of active duty.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>A veteran</strong>24 continuous months, or the full period you were called to active duty (at least 90 days), or less if discharged for a service-connected disability.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Guard and Reserve</strong>90 days of qualifying active duty, or 6 creditable years if you still serve, left honorably or retired.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>A surviving spouse</strong>Some surviving spouses can get a COE too. We find out which rule covers you.</span></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much you can borrow</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">With full entitlement there is <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-limits/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">no VA loan limit</a>. The lender decides how much you can borrow, and the appraisal must support the price.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you still have a VA loan on another home, the VA uses the county limit to work out what you have left. The current figure for a one-unit home in Horry and Georgetown counties is $832,750. After you sell the home and pay off the VA loan, you can ask the VA to restore your entitlement.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Credit and down payment help</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The VA requires no minimum credit score, but some lenders have their own. SC Housing's VA loans with no down payment need a score of 640.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Palmetto Heroes, SC Housing's $10,000 program for veterans, active-duty military and National Guard members, is closed. Its last round filled in about four weeks. SC Housing's year-round help works with a VA loan; our <a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to SC Housing's programs</a> gives its limits.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="va-loan-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">VA loan questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use a VA loan on a condo in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only in a condo community the VA has approved. Horry County has about 175 on the VA's list, but just 2 of the 29 oceanfront resort buildings in our directory are among them.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I have to live in the home with a VA loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. You certify that you intend to move in, and most lenders want you in the home within 60 days. A beach house you visit or a home you rent out does not count.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do 100 percent disabled veterans pay property tax in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not on the home they live in, once the VA rates them 100 percent permanently and totally disabled from their service. It covers the home, up to 5 acres and up to two cars. You apply to the SC Department of Revenue after the county grants the 4 percent rate.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I pay the VA funding fee if I have a disability rating?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No, if you receive VA compensation for a service-connected disability, or are eligible for it but receive retirement or active-duty pay instead.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use a VA loan more than once?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Once you have sold the home and paid off the VA loan, the VA can restore your entitlement when you ask. With a VA loan still open on another home, you may have entitlement left for a second one.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What interest rate will I get on a VA loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lender quotes your rate. We do not quote rates. We can introduce you to our preferred lender, or you can use any lender you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://lgy.va.gov/lgyhub/condo-report" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA condo report</a>, <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/condlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD FHA condo list</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA purchase loans</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA funding fee</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-limits/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA loan limits</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-37</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/PT401I.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR PT-401-I</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County 2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/charleston-health-care/locations/myrtle-beach-va-clinic/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach VA Clinic</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2024.B21001?g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>. Homes for sale: Chapter3's count of MLS listings, in aggregate. Drive times: OpenStreetMap routing, no traffic. Not loan or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped and resized the photo.</div><div role="listitem">Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach. Photo: Carol M. Highsmith, <a href="https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/res/482_high.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://www.loc.gov/item/2017880876/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Library of Congress</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped the left side of this photo to a 16:9 frame and resized it.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, the kind of building that is rarely on the VA's list","caption":"Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, the kind of building that is rarely on the VA's list.","description":"A row of oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach with stacked balconies and pools behind the dunes, seen from a plane over the ocean","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"U.S. Geological Survey"},"creditText":"U.S","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (U.S. Geological Survey)","license":"https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX","isBasedOn":"https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Oceanfront, central Myrtle Beach, Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true},{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/imag