aps & Routes City Events List Conventions Golf Cart Laws Host a Special Event Rent a Facility SC's Largest Garage Sale Tents & Umbrellas Military Appreciation Days Vacation Information Go Home More News New plaques at the Wall of Service at Warbird Park New plaques at the Wall of Service at Warbird Park Check out these new plaques at the Wall of Service at Myrtle Beach’s Warbird Park. The wall and the park remember the history of the Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, which closed in 1993. Military and civilian personnel who served at the base may have their names and dates listed on the Wall of Service. Eagle Scout Cole Smith provided an easy-to-use online look-up system to find a name by column and row, along with links to videos about the people, places and planes of the former Air Force Base. He and fellow scouts also improved the park’s landscaping. For more information, including links, visit https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/.../wall_of_service.php . City of Myrtle Beach P.O. Box 2468 Myrtle Beach, SC 29578 info@cityofmyrtlebeach.com Powered By Revize Login × Share this page Copy and past this code into your website. <a href="http://cms5.revize.com/revize/troymi/">Your Link Name</a> Share this page on your favorite Social network Facebook Twitter Google Plus Reddit Close 
