+ Veterans Affairs - Horry County SC.Gov Skip to main content Government Administrator Appointed and Elected Officials Boards and Commissions Code of Ordinances County Council Departments Business Bid Opportunities Business License Hospitality Fee Register of Deeds Tax Payer Services Zoning Compliance Residents 311 Service Request Council Meetings & Agendas Flooding & Disaster Prep Land Info Tax Payer Services Things to Do Sign in Login Register Veterans Affairs FAQs Contact More Info General Info Burial Information VA Healthcare Enrollment Military Discharge Presumptives Agent Orange Gulf War Illness Camp Lejeune Water Checklists Compensation Checklist Pension Checklist Other Reservist Benefits Flag Flying Home Departments Veterans Affairs Honorably serving those who served and sacrificed for this great nation Our Mission The mission of the Horry County Veterans Affairs Office is to provide education and assistance on the multitude of programs and benefits sponsored by the United States Department of Veterans Affairs. The education is made available to the general public but is predominantly for Veterans, surviving spouses, dependents and beneficiaries that we serve. We provide our clients assistance with claim filing for benefits they are eligible for, advice and representation on the VA appeal system and assistance with enrollment in the VA medical system. Our Vision Within the next five years the Horry County Veterans Affairs Office will become a model for all County Veterans Affairs Offices in the state of South Carolina. We will engage in a culture of excellence by providing Veterans and survivors with accurate information on VA benefits and programs; treat all clients with dignity and respect; respond timely to all communication; provide innovative computer service for Veterans to electronically enroll in VA programs and continually increase our knowledge on the multitude of VA benefits. Our Values As a department in Horry County government, we value honesty, respect, service to country, patriotism, sacrifice and personal excellence. We acknowledge, respect and honor all Veterans for their service to America no matter how, when or where they served. We proudly pledge ourselves to creating and maintaining a customer service environment for Veterans and their survivors. We hold ourselves accountable to our customers, partners and each other. We have a passion for Veterans and firmly believe that excellence is not a goal, it is the standard. Contact Us Name Email Phone Number Submit Veterans Affairs (843) 915-5480 (843) 915-6480 PGEgaHJlZj0nbWFpbHRvOmhjZy5WZXRlcmFuc0FmZmFpcnNAaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3YnPmhjZy5WZXRlcmFuc0FmZmFpcnNAaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3Y8L2E+ HOURS Monday–Friday 8am–5pm Location 1949 Industrial Park Rd Suite 101 Conway, SC 29526 Mailing 1949 Industrial Park Rd Suite 101 Conway, SC 29526 www.horrycountysc.gov | HC Government A product of Horry County Government ©2026 by Horry County Government — All Rights Reserved. General Info PGEgaHJlZj0nbWFpbHRvOmluZm9AaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3YnPmluZm9AaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3Y8L2E+ Departments Employment News Online Services Search Site Map Tax Payer Services Legal Accessibility Statement Privacy Terms 
