+<h2>Motor Vehicle Refund Requirements</h2>
+<h4>THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION IS REQUIRED BEFORE THE REFUND OF TAXES ON MOTOR VEHICLES CAN BE REFUNDED</h4>
+<h4 style="margin-top: 0;">SC TAX CODE, SECTION 12-37-2725b</h4>
+
+<div id="" class="two-column " style=" --column-gap: 4rem;">
+  <div class="column">
+
+
+<h6>PROPERTY TAX REFUND ON SOLD VEHICLE</h6>
+<ul>
+<li>Bill of Sale or copy of trade-in-agreement, copy of the original title(signed over to the new owner)</li>
+<li>Copy of paid tax receipt</li>
+<li>SC DMV form 5051</li>
+</ul>
+<h6>TAX REFUND ON A WRECKED VEHICLE</h6>
+<ul>
+<li>A statement from the insurance company, on company letterhead, stating the date of the accident, VIN, and the date the insurance company purchased the vehicle.</li>
+<li>Copy of paid tax receipt</li>
+<li>SC DMV form 5051</li>
+</ul></div>
+  <div class="column">
+
+
+<h6>TAX REFUND ON REPOSSESSED VEHICLE </h6>
+<ul>
+<li>A statement from the repo company printed on company letterhead stating the date of repossession, VIN, and the date the vehicle was sold.</li>
+<li>Paid tax receipt</li>
+<li>SC DMV form 5051</li>
+</ul>
+<h6>TAX REFUND DUE TO MOVING OUT OF STATE</h6>
+<ul>
+<li>Copy of new out-of-state registration</li>
+<li>Paid tax receipt </li>
+<li>SC DMV form 5051</li>
+</ul></div>
+</div>
