+        <div id="collapse-31351" class="accordion-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-31351">
+          <div class="accordion-body">
+            
+            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-html-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><dl class="ckeditor-accordion"><dt>If property is transferred to a government agency, and it is used for a general purpose for the public, does it&nbsp;​qualify for an exemption in the year of acquisition?</dt><dd><p>Yes, it does qualify if the property is transferred before the auditor opens the tax books in September.</p></dd><dt>If a church owns a parcel of property that is not contiguous to the actual church, and an income producing venture is located on the property, would the property qualify for an exemption from Property Taxes?</dt><dd><p>No, income producing property owned by a church does not qualify for an exemption from Property Taxes.</p></dd></dl></div>
