nu"><va-icon icon="close" size="3" class="vads-u-color--gray-dark"></va-icon></button><div class="vads-u-display--flex vads-u-align-items--center left-side-nav-title"><va-icon icon="home" size="3" class="hub-icon vads-u-color--white vads-u-display--flex vads-u-align-items--center vads-u-justify-content--center vads-u-margin-right--1 vads-u-background-color--hub-housing"></va-icon><h4 id="sidebar_header">Housing assistance</h4></div><div class="sidenav-previous-page"><a href="/housing-assistance/home-loans">VA-backed home loans</a></div><ul class="usa-sidenav-list"><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types">Loan types</a><ul class="usa-sidenav-sub_list"><li><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan">Purchase loan</a></li><li><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/native-american-direct-loan">Native American Direct Loan</a></li><li><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/interest-rate-reduction-loan">Interest rate reduction refinance loan</a></li><li><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/cash-out-loan">Cash-out refinance loan</a></li></ul></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility">Eligibility</a></li><li class="active-level"><a class="usa-current" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe">How to request a COE</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe-esp">Cómo solicitar un COE</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/request-coe-form-26-1880">Request a COE online</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/check-coe-status">Check your COE status</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/claim-or-appeal-status">Check claim, decision review, or appeal status</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/decision-reviews">Request a decision review</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-limits">Home loan limits</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs">Funding fee and closing costs</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://www.benefits.va.gov/homeloans/realtors_property_mgmt.asp">Find VA-acquired properties</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/home-buying-process">Buying a home with a VA-backed loan</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://news.va.gov/43234/va-and-the-consumer-financial-protection-bureau-warn-against-home-loan-refinancing-offers-that-sound-too-good-to-be-true/">Warning about refinancing offers</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://www.benefits.va.gov/HOMELOANS/documents/docs/va_policy_regarding_natural_disasters.pdf">Guidance on natural disasters</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/trouble-making-payments">VA help to avoid foreclosure</a></li></ul></div></nav><div class="va-btn-sidebarnav-trigger"><div class="sidenav-trigger-sentinel"></div><div class="" id="sidenav-trigger"><button aria-controls="va-detailpage-sidebar"><strong>In this section</strong><va-icon icon="menu" size="3" class="vads-u-color--link-default"></va-icon></button></div></div><div class="vads-grid-row"><div class="vads-grid-col-12"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)","headline":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)","description":"Find out how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to prove to your lender that you qualify for a VA direct or VA-backed home loan based on your service history and duty status. Then, learn more about the rest of the loan application process.","url":"https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe/"}</script><article class="usa-content vads-u-padding-bottom--0"><div data-widget-type="i18-select"></div><h1>How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)</h1><div class="va-introtext"><p>Learn how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE). This is the first step in getting a VA-backed home loan or Native American Direct Loan. It confirms for your lender that you qualify for the VA home loan benefit. Then, choose your loan type and learn about the rest of the loan application process.</p>
+</div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a_section"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I prepare before I start a COE request?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>Gather the information you’ll need to request a COE. Select the description here that matches you best to find out what you’ll need.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"/family-and-caregiver-benefits/housing-assistance/surviving-spouse-home-loan\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"93b3819f-f40e-4cf0-89ea-5638434b8599\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Home loans for surviving spouses\">Find out how to request a COE as a surviving spouse\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}}]}</script><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="how-do-i-prepare-before-i-star">How do I prepare before I start a COE request?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>Gather the information you’ll need to request a COE. Select the description here that matches you best to find out what you’ll need.</p></div></div><div id="b791dfc5-0b69-4623-aea1-be4a92691f0a" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel" data-entity-id="4990"><va-accordion><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="veteran-cdd83043-50ad-4ac5-b167-75470b193f35"><h3 slot="headline">Veteran</h3><div id="cdd83043-50ad-4ac5-b167-75470b193f35" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4991" data-analytics-faq-text="Veteran"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4991"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a Veteran</strong>, you’ll need a copy of your discharge or separation papers (DD214).</p></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="service-member-f70baf4b-fbcf-4638-939d-b4f4a9ae09d0"><h3 slot="headline">Service member</h3><div id="f70baf4b-fbcf-4638-939d-b4f4a9ae09d0" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4992" data-analytics-faq-text="Service member"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4992"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re an active-duty service member</strong>, you’ll need a statement of service—signed by your commander, adjutant, or personnel officer—showing this information:</p><ul><li>Your full name</li><li>Your Social Security number</li><li>Your date of birth</li><li>The date you entered duty</li><li>The duration of any lost time</li><li>The name of the command providing the information</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="current-or-former-activated-national-guard-member-608f18e0-9f85-4de7-98b8-bed123177892"><h3 slot="headline">Current or former activated National Guard member</h3><div id="608f18e0-9f85-4de7-98b8-bed123177892" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4993" data-analytics-faq-text="Current or former activated National Guard member"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4993"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a current or former activated National Guard member</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>you’ll need a copy of your DD214 or other discharge documents.</p><p><strong>If you’re a current or former activated National Guard member with at least 90 days of active-duty service including at least 30 consecutive days</strong>, you’ll need a copy of 1 of these documents that shows your activation date:</p><ul><li>Your DD214 that shows 32 USC sections 316, 502, 503, 504, or 505 activation, <strong>or</strong></li><li>An annual point statement, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Your DD220 with accompanying orders</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="current-or-former-activated-reserve-member-e5660f79-a008-45c3-b4aa-a0fbc0085601"><h3 slot="headline">Current or former activated Reserve member</h3><div id="e5660f79-a008-45c3-b4aa-a0fbc0085601" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="100602" data-analytics-faq-text="Current or former activated Reserve member"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-100602"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a current or former activated Reserve member</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>you’ll need a copy of your DD214 or other discharge documents.</p></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="current-member-of-the-national-guard-or-reserve-who-has-neve-855729b9-6286-420d-a687-c4d7aa3345f0"><h3 slot="headline">Current member of the National Guard or Reserve who has never been activated</h3><div id="855729b9-6286-420d-a687-c4d7aa3345f0" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4994" data-analytics-faq-text="Current member of the National Guard or Reserve who has never been activated"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4994"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a current member of the National Guard or Reserve and have&nbsp;never been activated</strong>, you’ll need a statement of service—signed by your commander, adjutant, or personnel officer—showing this information:</p><ul><li>Your full name</li><li>Your Social Security number</li><li>Your date of birth</li><li>The date you entered duty</li><li>Your total number of creditable years of service</li><li>The duration of any lost time</li><li>The name of the command providing the information</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="discharged-member-of-the-national-guard-who-was-never-activa-5ccaf71b-4e7a-4083-81e5-9d936a4c275e"><h3 slot="headline">Discharged member of the National Guard who was never activated</h3><div id="5ccaf71b-4e7a-4083-81e5-9d936a4c275e" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4995" data-analytics-faq-text="Discharged member of the National Guard who was never activated"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4995"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a discharged member of the National Guard and were never activated</strong>, you’ll need this information:</p><ul><li>Your Report of Separation and Record of Service (NGB Form 22) for each period of National Guard service, <strong>and</strong></li><li>Your Retirement Points Statement (NGB Form 23) and proof of the character of service</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="discharged-member-of-the-reserve-who-was-never-activated-3b65328b-ed54-49b3-94f2-f14e2040d9da"><h3 slot="headline">Discharged member of the Reserve who was never activated</h3><div id="3b65328b-ed54-49b3-94f2-f14e2040d9da" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4996" data-analytics-faq-text="Discharged member of the Reserve who was never activated"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4996"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a discharged member of the Reserve and were never activated</strong>, you’ll need this information:</p><ul><li>A copy of your latest annual retirement points, <strong>and</strong></li><li>Proof of your honorable service</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="surviving-spouse-of-a-veteran-who-died-on-active-duty-or-who-91257eac-c97b-4741-8aec-96871ccfe75f"><h3 slot="headline">Surviving spouse of a Veteran who died on active duty or who had a service-connected disability</h3><div id="91257eac-c97b-4741-8aec-96871ccfe75f" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="4997" data-analytics-faq-text="Surviving spouse of a Veteran who died on active duty or who had a service-connected disability"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-4997"><div itemProp="text"><p><strong>If you’re a surviving spouse</strong> who qualifies for home loan benefits, you’ll need the Veteran’s discharge documents (DD214)—if available—and:</p><p><strong>If you’re receiving Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.)</strong>, you’ll need to fill out and send us a Request for Determination of Loan Guaranty Eligibility—Unmarried Surviving Spouses (VA Form 26-1817).</p><p><a href="/forms/26-1817" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="925a1c05-c200-4abb-af75-32f3af25f1ef" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="VA Form 26-1817">Get VA Form 26-1817 to download</a></p><p><strong>Or</strong></p><p><strong>If you’re not receiving Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.)</strong>, you’ll need to send us all of these documents:</p><ul><li>A completed Application for D.I.C., Death Pension and/or Accrued Benefits (VA Form 21P-534EZ), <strong>and</strong></li><li>A copy of your marriage license, <strong>and</strong></li><li>The Veteran’s death certificate</li></ul><p><a href="/forms/21p-534ez" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="3c37a3e1-65d5-4add-b46b-a6c0f522e276" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="VA Form 21P-534EZ">Get VA Form 21P-534EZ to download</a></p><p><a href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="93a096d5-1c1a-4248-bad0-816a22fd13c3" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Eligibility for VA home loan programs">Find out if you qualify for home loan benefits</a></p><p><a href="https://www.archives.gov/veterans/military-service-records/">Get military service records online</a></p></div></div></div></va-accordion-item></va-accordion></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p><a href="/family-and-caregiver-benefits/housing-assistance/surviving-spouse-home-loan" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="93b3819f-f40e-4cf0-89ea-5638434b8599" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Home loans for surviving spouses">Find out how to request a COE as a surviving spouse</a></p></div></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h2 id="how-do-i-request-a-coe">How do I request a COE?</h2><p>You can request a COE in any of these 3 ways.</p><h3>Option 1: Online</h3><p><va-link-action href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/request-coe-form-26-1880" text="Request a COE" type="primary" /></p></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h3>Option 2: Through your lender</h3><p>Your lender may be able to use an online system (called Web LGY) to get your COE. Ask your lender about this option.</p><h3>Option 3: By mail</h3><p>To request a COE by mail, fill out a Request for a Certificate of Eligibility (VA Form 26-1880) and mail it to the address for your regional loan center.&nbsp;You can find the address on the last page of the form. Note that mail requests may take longer than requesting a COE online or through your lender.</p><p><a href="/forms/26-1880" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="e93e79cd-4ce5-46e0-821a-cb09ac146fa8" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="VA Form 26-1880">Get VA Form 26-1880 to download</a></p></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h2 id="what-happens-after-i-request-a">What happens after I request a COE?</h2><p>We’ll review your request and tell you our decision. You can check the status of your request online.</p><p><a href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/check-coe-status" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="cb745b8c-d52e-4be2-9443-eb04c1738998" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Check the status of your VA home loan COE">Learn how to check the status of your home loan COE</a></p><h3 id="next-steps-for-getting-a-va-di">Next steps for getting a VA direct or VA-backed home loan</h3><p>Requesting a COE is only part of the process for getting a VA direct or VA-backed home loan. Your next steps will depend on the type of loan and the lender. (For most loans, the lender is a private bank or mortgage company. For the Native American Direct Loan, we’re the lender).</p><p>The lender will request a&nbsp;VA&nbsp;appraisal (assessment) of the house. An appraisal estimates the house’s market value at the time of inspection. An appraisal isn’t a home inspection or a guaranty of value.</p><p>The lender will review the appraisal and your credit and income information.&nbsp;If they decide to accept your application, they’ll work&nbsp;with you to select a title company (or other entity) to close&nbsp;(transfer ownership) on the house.</p></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a_section"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I have questions about the loan process?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>If you have any questions that your lender can’t answer, you can call us at&nbsp;\u003cva-telephone contact=\"877-827-3702\" extension=\"\">\u003c/va-telephone>&nbsp;(TTY: 711)&nbsp;to talk to a VA home loan representative. We’re here Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. ET.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3gR_BmMP7A\">Play a YouTube video about VA home loans and how to apply\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}}]}</script><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="what-if-i-have-questions-about">What if I have questions about the loan process?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>If you have any questions that your lender can’t answer, you can call us at&nbsp;<va-telephone contact="877-827-3702" extension=""></va-telephone>&nbsp;(TTY: 711)&nbsp;to talk to a VA home loan representative. We’re here Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. ET.</p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3gR_BmMP7A">Play a YouTube video about VA home loans and how to apply</a></p></div></div></div></div><div class="va-nav-linkslist va-nav-linkslist--related"><section data-template="paragraphs/list_of_link_teasers" data-entity-id="5a6ee667-a472-4ad7-aa6e-7f0bb60efd20"><h2 id="loan-options" class="vads-u-border-bottom--1px vads-u-border-color--base-light vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-padding-top--2 vads-u-padding-bottom--0p5">Loan options</h2><ul class="usa-unstyled-list"><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="ab547200-40ec-451c-825f-d8799d97fa62" data-links-list-header="Purchase loan" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/" target="" text="Purchase loan"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Find out how to get a VA-backed purchase loan to buy a home.</p></li><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="7275121d-b6e4-4815-9b9c-aa02ab456d24" data-links-list-header="Interest rate reduction refinance loan (IRRRL)" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/interest-rate-reduction-loan/" target="" text="Interest rate reduction refinance loan (IRRRL)"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Find out how to get an IRRRL loan to refinance an existing loan.</p></li><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="7d03b2d7-f1f5-4f75-bee8-5120dd74c385" data-links-list-header="Cash-out refinance loan" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/cash-out-loan/" target="" text="Cash-out refinance loan"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Learn how to get cash from your home equity to pay off debts, pay for school, or take care of other needs.</p></li><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="65c4f46f-bcd1-4be5-ae9f-af8279fd5404" data-links-list-header="Native American Direct Loan (NADL)" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/native-american-direct-loan/" target="" text="Native American Direct Loan (NADL)"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Find out if you can get a NADL loan to buy, build, or improve a home on federal trust land.</p></li></ul></section></div><va-back-to-top></va-back-to-top><div data-testid="content-footer" class="last-updated "><div class="mobile-lg:vads-u-display--flex above-footer-elements-container"><div class="vads-u-flex--auto"><span class="vads-u-text-align--justify"><p>Last updated: <time dateTime="2026-09-22">September 22, 2026</time></p></span></div><div class="vads-u-flex--1 vads-u-text-align--right"><va-button id="mdFormButton" disable-analytics="" secondary="" class="vads-u-background-color--white" text="Feedback"></va-button></div></div></div></article></div></div></div></div></div></main><footer class="footer"><div id="footerNav" data-testid="footer" data-minimal-footer="false"></div></footer><div id="logout-modal-root"></div></div><script id="__NEXT_DATA__" type="application/json" nonce="JH5uCgskatFyTPDzlFvPcunt9FmFP0xg">{"props":{"pageProps":{"previewTokenError":false,"preview":false,"serializedResource":{"data":{"id":"61f76c4d-0631-48d1-8706-bbf1354c71dc","entityId":754,"entityPath":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe","type":"node--page","published":true,"moderationState":"published","title":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)","metatags":[{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"title","content":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE) | Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"description","content":"Learn how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE). This is the first step in getting a VA-backed home loan or Native American Direct Loan. It confirms for your lender that you qualify for the VA home loan benefit. Then, choose your loan type and learn about the rest of the loan application process."}},{"tag":"link","attributes":{"rel":"image_src","href":"https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:site_name","content":"Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:title","content":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE) | Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:description","content":"Learn how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE). This is the first step in getting a VA-backed home loan or Native American Direct Loan. It confirms for your lender that you qualify for the VA home loan benefit. Then, choose your loan type and learn about the rest of the loan application process."}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:image","content":"https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:image:alt","content":"U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:card","content":"summary_large_image"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:site","content":"@DeptVetAffairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:description","content":"Find out how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to prove to your lender that you qualify for a VA direct or VA-backed home loan based on your service history and duty status. Then, learn more about the rest of the loan application process."}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:title","content":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE) | Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:image:alt","content":"U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:image","content":"https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png"}}],"breadcrumbs":[{"href":"/","label":"Home"},{"href":"/housing-assistance","label":"Housing assistance"},{"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans","label":"VA-backed home loans"},{"href":"","label":"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)"}],"lastUpdated":"2026-09-22T19:31:12+00:00","description":"Find out how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to prove to your lender that you qualify for a VA direct or VA-backed home loan based on your service history and duty status. Then, learn more about the rest of the loan application process.","introText":"\u003cp\u003eLearn how to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE). This is the first step in getting a VA-backed home loan or Native American Direct Loan. It confirms for your lender that you qualify for the VA home loan benefit. Then, choose your loan type and learn about the rest of the loan application process.\u003c/p\u003e\n","showTableOfContents":false,"alert":null,"featuredContent":[],"mainContent":[{"header":null,"intro":null,"questions":[{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"How do I prepare before I start a COE request?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"5ed0e03a-acb4-40a1-a90c-089509ae1e8c","html":"\u003cp\u003eGather the information you’ll need to request a COE. Select the description here that matches you best to find out what you’ll need.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel","id":"b791dfc5-0b69-4623-aea1-be4a92691f0a","entityId":4990,"paragraphs":[{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"cdd83043-50ad-4ac5-b167-75470b193f35","entityId":4991,"title":"Veteran","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a Veteran\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need a copy of your discharge or separation papers (DD214).\u003c/p\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"f70baf4b-fbcf-4638-939d-b4f4a9ae09d0","entityId":4992,"title":"Service member","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re an active-duty service member\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need a statement of service—signed by your commander, adjutant, or personnel officer—showing this information:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour full name\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Social Security number\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour date of birth\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe date you entered duty\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe duration of any lost time\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe name of the command providing the information\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"608f18e0-9f85-4de7-98b8-bed123177892","entityId":4993,"title":"Current or former activated National Guard member","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a current or former activated National Guard member\u003c/strong\u003e,\u003cstrong\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/strong\u003eyou’ll need a copy of your DD214 or other discharge documents.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a current or former activated National Guard member with at least 90 days of active-duty service including at least 30 consecutive days\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need a copy of 1 of these documents that shows your activation date:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour DD214 that shows 32 USC sections 316, 502, 503, 504, or 505 activation, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAn annual point statement, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour DD220 with accompanying orders\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"e5660f79-a008-45c3-b4aa-a0fbc0085601","entityId":100602,"title":"Current or former activated Reserve member","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a current or former activated Reserve member\u003c/strong\u003e,\u003cstrong\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/strong\u003eyou’ll need a copy of your DD214 or other discharge documents.\u003c/p\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"855729b9-6286-420d-a687-c4d7aa3345f0","entityId":4994,"title":"Current member of the National Guard or Reserve who has never been activated","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a current member of the National Guard or Reserve and have\u0026nbsp;never been activated\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need a statement of service—signed by your commander, adjutant, or personnel officer—showing this information:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour full name\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Social Security number\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour date of birth\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe date you entered duty\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour total number of creditable years of service\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe duration of any lost time\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe name of the command providing the information\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"5ccaf71b-4e7a-4083-81e5-9d936a4c275e","entityId":4995,"title":"Discharged member of the National Guard who was never activated","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a discharged member of the National Guard and were never activated\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need this information:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Report of Separation and Record of Service (NGB Form 22) for each period of National Guard service, \u003cstrong\u003eand\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Retirement Points Statement (NGB Form 23) and proof of the character of service\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"3b65328b-ed54-49b3-94f2-f14e2040d9da","entityId":4996,"title":"Discharged member of the Reserve who was never activated","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a discharged member of the Reserve and were never activated\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need this information:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eA copy of your latest annual retirement points, \u003cstrong\u003eand\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eProof of your honorable service\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"91257eac-c97b-4741-8aec-96871ccfe75f","entityId":4997,"title":"Surviving spouse of a Veteran who died on active duty or who had a service-connected disability","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re a surviving spouse\u003c/strong\u003e who qualifies for home loan benefits, you’ll need the Veteran’s discharge documents (DD214)—if available—and:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re receiving Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.)\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need to fill out and send us a Request for Determination of Loan Guaranty Eligibility—Unmarried Surviving Spouses (VA Form 26-1817).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/forms/26-1817\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"925a1c05-c200-4abb-af75-32f3af25f1ef\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"VA Form 26-1817\"\u003eGet VA Form 26-1817 to download\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOr\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you’re not receiving Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.)\u003c/strong\u003e, you’ll need to send us all of these documents:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eA completed Application for D.I.C., Death Pension and/or Accrued Benefits (VA Form 21P-534EZ), \u003cstrong\u003eand\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eA copy of your marriage license, \u003cstrong\u003eand\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Veteran’s death certificate\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/forms/21p-534ez\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"3c37a3e1-65d5-4add-b46b-a6c0f522e276\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"VA Form 21P-534EZ\"\u003eGet VA Form 21P-534EZ to download\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"93a096d5-1c1a-4248-bad0-816a22fd13c3\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Eligibility for VA home loan programs\"\u003eFind out if you qualify for home loan benefits\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.archives.gov/veterans/military-service-records/\"\u003eGet military service records online\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","paragraphs":[]}],"bordered":false},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"1971f3b8-646f-4648-9ea0-adb85148398d","html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/family-and-caregiver-benefits/housing-assistance/surviving-spouse-home-loan\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"93b3819f-f40e-4cf0-89ea-5638434b8599\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Home loans for surviving spouses\"\u003eFind out how to request a COE as a surviving spouse\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"a3776036-1b58-44e6-bc00-93871562907e"}],"displayAccordion":false,"type":"paragraph--q_a_section","id":"3f5d3769-1e04-4aa8-9c5d-6f52692c3f3e"},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"8ac13512-8d57-4454-8995-091341b12578","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"how-do-i-request-a-coe\"\u003eHow do I request a COE?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou can request a COE in any of these 3 ways.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eOption 1: Online\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cva-link-action href=\"https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/request-coe-form-26-1880\" text=\"Request a COE\" type=\"primary\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"80624cf2-820f-443e-8406-02e60cd182c0","html":"\u003ch3\u003eOption 2: Through your lender\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour lender may be able to use an online system (called Web LGY) to get your COE. Ask your lender about this option.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eOption 3: By mail\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo request a COE by mail, fill out a Request for a Certificate of Eligibility (VA Form 26-1880) and mail it to the address for your regional loan center.\u0026nbsp;You can find the address on the last page of the form. Note that mail requests may take longer than requesting a COE online or through your lender.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/forms/26-1880\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"e93e79cd-4ce5-46e0-821a-cb09ac146fa8\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"VA Form 26-1880\"\u003eGet VA Form 26-1880 to download\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"396b98c0-7d19-44a8-a5ae-583c85e860d8","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"what-happens-after-i-request-a\"\u003eWhat happens after I request a COE?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe’ll review your request and tell you our decision. You can check the status of your request online.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/housing-assistance/home-loans/check-coe-status\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"cb745b8c-d52e-4be2-9443-eb04c1738998\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Check the status of your VA home loan COE\"\u003eLearn how to check the status of your home loan COE\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"next-steps-for-getting-a-va-di\"\u003eNext steps for getting a VA direct or VA-backed home loan\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eRequesting a COE is only part of the process for getting a VA direct or VA-backed home loan. Your next steps will depend on the type of loan and the lender. (For most loans, the lender is a private bank or mortgage company. For the Native American Direct Loan, we’re the lender).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe lender will request a\u0026nbsp;VA\u0026nbsp;appraisal (assessment) of the house. An appraisal estimates the house’s market value at the time of inspection. An appraisal isn’t a home inspection or a guaranty of value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe lender will review the appraisal and your credit and income information.\u0026nbsp;If they decide to accept your application, they’ll work\u0026nbsp;with you to select a title company (or other entity) to close\u0026nbsp;(transfer ownership) on the house.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"header":null,"intro":null,"questions":[{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"What if I have questions about the loan process?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"fb3ba71e-95cb-4e42-9058-59b638f70cf0","html":"\u003cp\u003eIf you have any questions that your lender can’t answer, you can call us at\u0026nbsp;\u003cva-telephone contact=\"877-827-3702\" extension=\"\"\u003e\u003c/va-telephone\u003e\u0026nbsp;(TTY: 711)\u0026nbsp;to talk to a VA home loan representative. We’re here Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. ET.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3gR_BmMP7A\"\u003ePlay a YouTube video about VA home loans and how to apply\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"7d99746f-de37-4b18-8e7b-920a9089f29e"}],"displayAccordion":false,"type":"paragraph--q_a_section","id":"aac3cbce-5f10-4e6b-a373-965f0ee0cdb7"}],"relatedLinks":{"type":"paragraph--list_of_link_teasers","id":"5a6ee667-a472-4ad7-aa6e-7f0bb60efd20","entityId":4982,"title":"Loan options","linkTeasers":[{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"ab547200-40ec-451c-825f-d8799d97fa62","entityId":4983,"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/","label":"Purchase loan","summary":"Find out how to get a VA-backed purchase loan to buy a home."},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"7275121d-b6e4-4815-9b9c-aa02