:null},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"647438fd-d294-435f-8feb-77f57e03eb03","entityId":34730,"href":"/charleston-health-care/billing-and-insurance/","label":"Check your billing, insurance, and payment options","summary":null},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"7681578a-3791-46bf-a861-8dae27d41250","entityId":34731,"href":"/charleston-health-care/work-with-us/volunteer-or-donate/","label":"Volunteer or donate","summary":null},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"754e5291-1e46-4503-ae3b-34a84f8c39a5","entityId":140734,"href":"/charleston-health-care/programs/fisher-house/","label":"Lodging for Patients and Families ","summary":null},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"526b02d0-c574-41b9-8f74-2a6161c37a1c","entityId":109835,"href":"/charleston-health-care/programs/military-sexual-trauma-mst/","label":"Military Sexual Trauma","summary":null},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"0137a02b-8271-4a23-b743-62c28674e7c8","entityId":195518,"href":"https://dvagov.sharepoint.com/sites/vhachahub/RHJVAMCSIM/_layouts/15/listforms.aspx?cid=OGQ0NGE4MjUtMGJjMS00NDRjLWIyZjYtODdjYjUwNDE1MDI2\u0026nav=YmYxNzg1NjQtMDIzYi00YWU3LWIwM2EtZGMzNjNiMmM1YzZl","label":"Simulation Center Reservation Form","summary":null},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"32556632-efde-4e57-94a6-5d1a6baf0808","entityId":201787,"href":"/charleston-health-care/programs/nutrition-and-food-services/","label":"Nutrition and Food Services","summary":"Learn about nutrition resources, Fresh Xpress events, recipes and cookbooks for Veterans. "}]},"locationServices":[{"title":"Parking","wysiwigContents":"\u003cp\u003eFree parking is available to all patients and visitors of the Charleston VAMC. On-site parking, and shuttle services are available. Please visit our\u0026nbsp;\u003ca data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"15e08f34-6474-4474-8f2a-d412956bffee\" href=\"/charleston-health-care/programs/parking\" title=\"Parking\"\u003eParking page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCost:\u003c/strong\u003e Free\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWheelchair availability:\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026nbsp; Wheelchairs are available upon arrival for patients who need them to access the building.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"title":"Interactive Campus Map","wysiwigContents":"\u003cp\u003eExplore and search an interactive map of the medical center. \u0026nbsp; Download the \u003ca href=\"http://vaapp-redirect.medrics.us/\"\u003eVA ME app\u003c/a\u003e on your smartphone and get real-time, turn-by-turn directions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e"},{"title":"Transportation services and schedules","wysiwigContents":"\u003ch4 dir=\"ltr\"\u003eVan services for Veterans\u003c/h4\u003e\n\n\u003ch5 dir=\"ltr\"\u003eDAV vans\u003c/h5\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026nbsp;Individual van schedules vary\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eWe work with Disabled American Veterans and county Veterans Affairs directors to provide transportation for Veterans and authorized caregivers to get to scheduled medical appointments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch5 dir=\"ltr\"\u003eNon-DAV van services\u003c/h5\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eMany localities in the region provide other van services to Veterans.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003ca data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"a91428ca-a1f4-458e-8e16-bf3c3b187fb6\" href=\"/charleston-health-care/dav-vans-transportation-for-veterans\" title=\"DAV vans: Transportation for Veterans\"\u003eLearn more about DAV and the other van services available in your\u0026nbsp;county\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eShuttle Service\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h4\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eThere is an off-site parking lease located at 41 Folly Rd. near Porter Gaud School (shown as P6 on the map on our \u003ca data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"15e08f34-6474-4474-8f2a-d412956bffee\" href=\"/charleston-health-care/programs/parking\" title=\"Parking\"\u003eparking page\u003c/a\u003e). The offsite parking provides 600 parking spaces, a covered non-smoking shelter, and shuttles that run from 4:30 a.m. until 11 p.m. Monday through Friday with the exception of holidays. Shuttles run every five minutes during peak hours of 6:00 - 8:30 a.m. and 3:00 - 5:30 p.m., and run every 15 minutes at other times of the day. The shuttle service is designed to ensure that rides to and from the VAMC are available when you need them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 dir=\"ltr\"\u003eBeneficiary travel\u003c/h4\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eBeneficiary travel benefits include round-trip transportation from your home to the medical center, mileage reimbursement, or special mode transport.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://www.va.gov/health-care/file-travel-pay-reimbursement/\"\u003eFind out if you qualify for beneficiary travel benefits\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},{"title":"Lodging for patients and families","wysiwigContents":"\u003ch4 dir=\"ltr\"\u003eFisher House\u003c/h4\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eA place for visiting families to stay, free of charge, while their loved ones receive inpatient medical care.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003ca data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"7599f3a8-9def-4900-aa75-dc650fd8dc2f\" href=\"/charleston-health-care/programs/fisher-house\" title=\"Fisher House\"\u003ePlease visit our Fisher House page for more information.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 dir=\"ltr\"\u003eVisit Charleston\u003c/h4\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eThe Charleston Area Convention \u0026amp; Visitors Bureau has up-to-date listings for area hotels, as well as activities, transportation, restaurants, shops and more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.charlestoncvb.com/\"\u003ehttps://www.charlestoncvb.com/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"socialLinks":{"regionNickname":"VA Charleston health care","links":[{"icon":"mail","href":"https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USVHA/subscriber/new?topic_id=USVHA_210","text":"Subscribe to VA Charleston health care news and announcements"},{"icon":"mail","href":"https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USVHA/subscriber/new?topic_id=USVHA_414","text":"Subscribe to VA Charleston health care emergency notifications"},{"icon":"adjust","href":"/charleston-health-care/operating-status/","text":"VA Charleston health care operating status"},{"icon":"facebook","href":"https://www.facebook.com/VAMCCharleston","text":"VA Charleston Healthcare System Facebook page"},{"icon":"x","href":"https://twitter.com/charlestonvahcs?lang=en","text":"VA Charleston Healthcare System at Twitter"},{"icon":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/charlestonvahcs/","text":"VA Charleston Healthcare System at Instagram"}]},"lovellVariant":null,"lovellSwitchPath":null,"vamcSystemTitle":"VA Charleston health care","healthServices":[{"name":"Anesthesia","fieldAlsoKnownAs":"","fieldCommonlyTreatedCondition":"","fieldReferralRequired":"2","fieldTricareDescription":null,"description":"The anesthesia service works to keep you comfortable, safe\u0026nbsp;and pain-free during surgical or screening procedures.","entityId":"544582e6-a613-4b3a-9164-115715d5b9e7","entityBundle":"health_care_local_health_service","fieldBody":"\u003cp\u003eOur specially trained doctors, called anesthesiologists, can help with your care before, during, and after surgery. They will develop a plan for your care and safety, provide medicine to keep you comfortable during your operation, and help you manage your pain after surgery. Our services include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGeneral anesthesia (intravenous drugs, inhaled gasses, or some combination) to keep you pain-free and in a sleep-like state during surgery or other medical procedures\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRegional anesthesia (injecting numbing drugs around nerves) to control pain in specific parts of your body during or after surgery\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMonitoring your breathing and vital body functions while you’re under anesthesia\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorking with the rest of your care team to manage your pain medications after your operation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCoordinating care with your other health care professionals to facilitate a smooth transition from hospital to home\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","isMentalHealthService":false,"locations":[{"type":"paragraph--service_location","id":"4054350e-b6f9-4091-a020-22d602263119","officeVisits":null,"virtualSupport":null,"apptIntroTextType":"use_default_text","apptIntroTextCustom":null,"appointmentPhoneNumbers":[],"onlineSchedulingAvail":null,"contactInfoPhoneNumbers":[],"emailContacts":[],"hours":"0","officeHours":[],"additionalHoursInfo":null,"useMainFacilityPhone":true,"useFacilityPhoneNumber":true,"serviceLocationAddress":{"type":"paragraph--service_location_address","id":"cbf88aef-8800-4680-87fd-3835507d3fd9","drupal_internal__id":46217,"drupal_internal__revision_id":1319768,"langcode":"en","status":true,"created":"2021-06-09T20:16:34+00:00","parent_id":"46218","parent_type":"paragraph","parent_field_name":"field_service_location_address","behavior_settings":[],"default_langcode":true,"revision_translation_affected":null,"breadcrumbs":[],"content_translation_source":"und","content_translation_outdated":false,"content_translation_changed":null,"field_address":{"langcode":null,"country_code":"US","administrative_area":"","locality":"","dependent_locality":null,"postal_code":"","sorting_code":null,"address_line1":"","address_line2":null},"field_building_name_number":null,"field_clinic_name":null,"field_use_facility_address":true,"field_wing_floor_or_room_number":null,"links":{"self":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/cbf88aef-8800-4680-87fd-3835507d3fd9?resourceVersion=id%3A1319768"},"working-copy":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/cbf88aef-8800-4680-87fd-3835507d3fd9?resourceVersion=rel%3Aworking-copy"}},"resourceIdObjMeta":{"target_revision_id":1319768,"drupal_internal__target_id":46217},"paragraph_type":{"type":"paragraphs_type--paragraphs_type","id":"bd794386-a382-48d0-84fb-47290c3c1176","resourceIdObjMeta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":"service_location_address"}},"relationshipNames":["paragraph_type"]}}],"fieldFacilityLocatorApiId":"vha_534","fieldHealthServiceApiId":"anesthesia"},{"name":"Audiology","fieldAlsoKnownAs":"Hearing and balance","fieldCommonlyTreatedCondition":"tinnitus, vertigo, hearing loss, vestibular conditions","fieldReferralRequired":"1","fieldTricareDescription":null,"description":"We diagnose and treat conditions affecting your hearing or balance, including hearing loss, tinnitus (noise or ringing in the ears) and dizziness.","entityId":"6fe1da43-4b95-41f4-a343-c773b3c90297","entityBundle":"health_care_local_health_service","fieldBody":"\u003cp\u003eOur Audiology and Speech Pathology clinic provides diagnostic and rehabilitative services, VA compensation and pension examinations, and screening for employee hearing conservation. We offer a full range of audiology and speech pathology services like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHearing and balance evaluations\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelection, management, and repair of hearing aids and assistive listening device assessments\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEvaluation, programming, and management of cochlear implants and bone-anchored implants\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEvaluation and treatment for auditory processing disorder\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eServices that help with speech, language, fluency, voice, cognitive communication, swallowing, stuttering, and laryngectomy (surgical removal of the larynx, which contains your vocal cords)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/health-care/order-hearing-aid-batteries-and-accessories\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"938ea13f-7872-41bc-8efe-9482713387f9\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Order hearing aid batteries and accessories from VA\"\u003eLearn more about VA hearing aids\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","isMentalHealthService":false,"locations":[{"type":"paragraph--service_location","id":"ec8820ca-9126-4c59-b09e-3eb1bcee991a","officeVisits":"yes_appointment_only","virtualSupport":"no","apptIntroTextType":"use_default_text","apptIntroTextCustom":null,"appointmentPhoneNumbers":[{"type":"paragraph--phone_number","id":"5aec28f2-357f-4f15-9594-30f7d67e9da9","entityId":152448,"label":"Audiology","number":"843-789-6495","extension":null,"phoneType":"tel"}],"onlineSchedulingAvail":"yes","contactInfoPhoneNumbers":[{"type":"paragraph--phone_number","id":"d0fe760c-d0b3-4f84-ad27-1b8f9cbe3853","entityId":108923,"label":"Audiology","number":"843-577-5011","extension":null,"phoneType":"tel"}],"emailContacts":[],"hours":"0","officeHours":[],"additionalHoursInfo":null,"useMainFacilityPhone":true,"useFacilityPhoneNumber":false,"serviceLocationAddress":{"type":"paragraph--service_location_address","id":"79980c58-2a2b-4bc9-908b-28883dd1d06e","drupal_internal__id":46219,"drupal_internal__revision_id":1946168,"langcode":"en","status":true,"created":"2021-06-09T20:16:34+00:00","parent_id":"46220","parent_type":"paragraph","parent_field_name":"field_service_location_address","behavior_settings":[],"default_langcode":true,"revision_translation_affected":true,"breadcrumbs":[],"content_translation_source":"und","content_translation_outdated":false,"content_translation_changed":null,"field_address":{"langcode":"en","country_code":"US","administrative_area":"","locality":"","dependent_locality":null,"postal_code":"","sorting_code":null,"address_line1":"","address_line2":""},"field_building_name_number":null,"field_clinic_name":null,"field_use_facility_address":true,"field_wing_floor_or_room_number":null,"links":{"self":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/79980c58-2a2b-4bc9-908b-28883dd1d06e?resourceVersion=id%3A1946168"},"working-copy":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/79980c58-2a2b-4bc9-908b-28883dd1d06e?resourceVersion=rel%3Aworking-copy"}},"resourceIdObjMeta":{"target_revision_id":1946168,"drupal_internal__target_id":46219},"paragraph_type":{"type":"paragraphs_type--paragraphs_type","id":"bd794386-a382-48d0-84fb-47290c3c1176","resourceIdObjMeta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":"service_location_address"}},"relationshipNames":["paragraph_type"]}}],"fieldFacilityLocatorApiId":"vha_534","fieldHealthServiceApiId":"audiology"},{"name":"Bariatric surgery","fieldAlsoKnownAs":"Weight loss surgery","fieldCommonlyTreatedCondition":"","fieldReferralRequired":"1","fieldTricareDescription":null,"description":"Bariatric surgery is an approach to help you improve your health and quality of life by losing weight.","entityId":"f6067c2a-a0c7-4512-aac0-ad865d127329","entityBundle":"health_care_local_health_service","fieldBody":"\u003cp\u003eBariatric surgery, also called weight-loss surgery, reduces the size of your stomach and small intestine to limit the amount of food you can eat or absorb. Bariatric surgery can be done in several ways, like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGastric bypass, which shrinks your stomach size and re-routes your digestive system, so you don’t absorb as much food\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSleeve gastrectomy, which removes part of your stomach, leaving only a slender “sleeve” that holds less food\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more visit our site \u003ca href=\"/charleston-health-care/programs/bariatric-surgery\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"936e4777-9eb2-4ae2-b9a6-ac4285526bb9\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Bariatric Surgery\"\u003ehere:\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","isMentalHealthService":false,"locations":[{"type":"paragraph--service_location","id":"0eb09652-4145-4408-8586-afa198b2b6a5","officeVisits":"yes_appointment_only","virtualSupport":null,"apptIntroTextType":"use_default_text","apptIntroTextCustom":null,"appointmentPhoneNumbers":[],"onlineSchedulingAvail":"yes","contactInfoPhoneNumbers":[],"emailContacts":[],"hours":"0","officeHours":[],"additionalHoursInfo":null,"useMainFacilityPhone":true,"useFacilityPhoneNumber":true,"serviceLocationAddress":{"type":"paragraph--service_location_address","id":"e1978bf3-c664-4039-8af1-261311e1e1c5","drupal_internal__id":46221,"drupal_internal__revision_id":1319776,"langcode":"en","status":true,"created":"2021-06-09T20:16:34+00:00","parent_id":"46222","parent_type":"paragraph","parent_field_name":"field_service_location_address","behavior_settings":[],"default_langcode":true,"revision_translation_affected":null,"breadcrumbs":[],"content_translation_source":"und","content_translation_outdated":false,"content_translation_changed":null,"field_address":{"langcode":"en","country_code":"US","administrative_area":"","locality":"","dependent_locality":null,"postal_code":"","sorting_code":null,"address_line1":"","address_line2":""},"field_building_name_number":null,"field_clinic_name":null,"field_use_facility_address":true,"field_wing_floor_or_room_number":null,"links":{"self":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/e1978bf3-c664-4039-8af1-261311e1e1c5?resourceVersion=id%3A1319776"},"working-copy":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/e1978bf3-c664-4039-8af1-261311e1e1c5?resourceVersion=rel%3Aworking-copy"}},"resourceIdObjMeta":{"target_revision_id":1319776,"drupal_internal__target_id":46221},"paragraph_type":{"type":"paragraphs_type--paragraphs_type","id":"bd794386-a382-48d0-84fb-47290c3c1176","resourceIdObjMeta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":"service_location_address"}},"relationshipNames":["paragraph_type"]}}],"fieldFacilityLocatorApiId":"vha_534","fieldHealthServiceApiId":"bariatricSurgery"},{"name":"Cancer care","fieldAlsoKnownAs":"","fieldCommonlyTreatedCondition":"","fieldReferralRequired":"2","fieldTricareDescription":"We offer expert cancer diagnosis and care. We can support you through treatment and beyond.","description":"VA provides expert cancer diagnosis and care. We offer services to support you through treatment and beyond.","entityId":"d23be2ac-93f7-43d3-be87-42dc4fcd3c4f","entityBundle":"health_care_local_health_service","fieldBody":"\u003cp\u003eIf you’re diagnosed with cancer, our team will work with you, your primary care doctor, and other health care providers to develop a specialized treatment plan. We offer personal, compassionate, and expert care, with services like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSurgical removal of tumors and other cancerous tissue\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eImmunotherapy, which helps your body’s natural defenses destroy cancer cells\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChemotherapy, which uses powerful drugs to fight cancer\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRadiotherapy, which uses high-energy radiation to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePalliative care, to reduce pain and control other symptoms and side effects, like nausea\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo read more about what we offer please \u003ca href=\"/charleston-health-care/programs/oncology\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"811b62f6-4573-4c6b-9c1a-c61011052b99\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Oncology\"\u003evisit our site here:\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","isMentalHealthService":false,"locations":[{"type":"paragraph--service_location","id":"8fbf4507-62d8-43e4-a8e6-7af71894470d","officeVisits":null,"virtualSupport":null,"apptIntroTextType":"use_default_text","apptIntroTextCustom":null,"appointmentPhoneNumbers":[],"onlineSchedulingAvail":null,"contactInfoPhoneNumbers":[],"emailContacts":[],"hours":"0","officeHours":[],"additionalHoursInfo":null,"useMainFacilityPhone":true,"useFacilityPhoneNumber":true,"serviceLocationAddress":{"type":"paragraph--service_location_address","id":"af3e8c4c-9df5-468d-816c-5c287fd8cfda","drupal_internal__id":46249,"drupal_internal__revision_id":1319805,"langcode":"en","status":true,"created":"2021-06-09T20:16:43+00:00","parent_id":"46250","parent_type":"paragraph","parent_field_name":"field_service_location_address","behavior_settings":[],"default_langcode":true,"revision_translation_affected":null,"breadcrumbs":[],"content_translation_source":"und","content_translation_outdated":false,"content_translation_changed":null,"field_address":{"langcode":null,"country_code":"US","administrative_area":"","locality":"","dependent_locality":null,"postal_code":"","sorting_code":null,"address_line1":"","address_line2":null},"field_building_name_number":null,"field_clinic_name":null,"field_use_facility_address":true,"field_wing_floor_or_room_number":null,"links":{"self":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/af3e8c4c-9df5-468d-816c-5c287fd8cfda?resourceVersion=id%3A1319805"},"working-copy":{"href":"https://prod.cms.va.gov/jsonapi/paragraph/service_location_address/af3e8c4c-9df5-468d-816c-5c287fd8cfda?resourceVersion=rel%3Aworking-copy"}},"resourceIdObjMeta":{"target_revision_id":1319805,"drupal_internal__target_id":46249},"paragraph_type":{"type":"paragraphs_type--paragraphs_type","id":"bd794386-a382-48d0-84fb-47290c3c1176","resourceIdObjMeta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":"service_location_address"}},"relationshipNames":["paragraph_type"]}}],"fieldFacilityLocatorApiId":"vha_534","fieldHealthServiceApiId":"cancer"},{"name":"Caregiver support","fieldAlsoKnownAs":"","fieldCommonlyTreatedCondition":"","fieldReferralRequired":"2","fieldTricareDescription":"If you're caring for someone with serious illness or disabilities, we can help you both. You may qualify for services like training, counseling, or respite care for when you need a break.","description":"If you are\u0026nbsp;caring for a Veteran with serious illness or disabilities, we can help you support them—and take care of yourself. You may qualify for services like training, counseling\u0026nbsp;or respite care when you need a break.","entityId":"6735bd18-6dd7-4d25-a96d-a517ed478cf0","entityBundle":"health_care_local_health_service","fieldBody":"\u003cp\u003eIf you’re a caregiver\u0026nbsp;for a Veteran, you can get support by contacting one of our caregiver support coordinators.\u0026nbsp;If the Veteran you care for was injured post-9/11, you may be eligible for even more services, including a stipend to help with expenses, training, and medical coverage if you aren’t already covered. For all caregivers, we can:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHelp you get caregiver assistance available through VA\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProvide progressive needs planning to help you manage degenerative conditions\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMatch you with services and benefits\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConnect you with local resources and programs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eListen to you when you struggle\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"52708fff-fd60-47db-bf84-a4702a105fcc\" href=\"/charleston-health-care/health-services/caregiver-support\" title=\"Caregiver support\"\u003eLearn more and connect with a support coordinator\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","isMentalHealthService":false,"locations":[{"type":"paragraph--service_location","id":"d688