assistance/home-loans/loan-limits">Home loan limits</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs">Funding fee and closing costs</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://www.benefits.va.gov/homeloans/realtors_property_mgmt.asp">Find VA-acquired properties</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/home-buying-process">Buying a home with a VA-backed loan</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://news.va.gov/43234/va-and-the-consumer-financial-protection-bureau-warn-against-home-loan-refinancing-offers-that-sound-too-good-to-be-true/">Warning about refinancing offers</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="https://www.benefits.va.gov/HOMELOANS/documents/docs/va_policy_regarding_natural_disasters.pdf">Guidance on natural disasters</a></li><li class=""><a class="" href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/trouble-making-payments">VA help to avoid foreclosure</a></li></ul></div></nav><div class="va-btn-sidebarnav-trigger"><div class="sidenav-trigger-sentinel"></div><div class="" id="sidenav-trigger"><button aria-controls="va-detailpage-sidebar"><strong>In this section</strong><va-icon icon="menu" size="3" class="vads-u-color--link-default"></va-icon></button></div></div><div class="vads-grid-row"><div class="vads-grid-col-12"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs","headline":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs","description":"Learn about VA home loan eligibility requirements. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify for a VA-backed loan based on your service history and duty status.","url":"https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility/"}</script><article class="usa-content vads-u-padding-bottom--0"><div data-widget-type="i18-select"></div><h1>Eligibility for VA home loan programs</h1><div class="va-introtext"><p>Learn about VA home loan eligibility requirements for a VA direct loan (Native American Direct Loan) or a VA-backed loan. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify based on your service history and duty status. To get financing for a VA-backed home loan, you must meet credit, income, and occupancy requirements from both us and your lender.</p>
+</div><div class="feature"><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="can-i-get-a-coe-for-a-native-a">Can I get a COE for a Native American Direct Loan or a VA-backed home loan?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>You may be able to get a COE if you meet the minimum active-duty service requirements for your service period or were discharged under a qualifying exception.</p></div></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h2 id="minimum-active-duty-service-re">Minimum active-duty service requirements</h2><h3>For service members</h3><p>If you’ve served for at least 90 continuous days (all at once, without a break in service), you meet the minimum active-duty service requirement.</p><h3>For Veterans</h3><p>The minimum active-duty service requirements depend on when you served.</p><h4>When did you serve?</h4></div></div><div id="b87aa60f-7bcc-4b02-b534-1099d5b61a32" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel" data-entity-id="109719"><va-accordion><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-august-2-1990-and-the-present-gulf-war-period-to-pre-14386229-a09d-4979-82e4-40718e5670d7"><h5 slot="headline">Between August 2, 1990, and the present (Gulf War period to present)</h5><div id="14386229-a09d-4979-82e4-40718e5670d7" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109708" data-analytics-faq-text="Between August 2, 1990, and the present (Gulf War period to present)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109708"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 24 continuous months,<strong> or</strong></li><li>The full period (at least 90 days) for which you were called or ordered to active duty, <strong>or</strong></li><li>At least 90 days if you were discharged under a qualifying exception, <strong>or</strong><br><a href="#what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu">Check the qualifying exceptions</a></li><li>Less than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-september-8-1980-and-august-1-1990-a554099d-a035-4291-b988-5d0b96545fbc"><h5 slot="headline"> Between September 8, 1980, and August 1, 1990</h5><div id="a554099d-a035-4291-b988-5d0b96545fbc" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109709" data-analytics-faq-text=" Between September 8, 1980, and August 1, 1990"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109709"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 24 continuous months, <strong>or</strong></li><li>The full period (at least 181 days) for which you were called to active duty, <strong>or</strong></li><li>At least 181 days if you were discharged under a qualifying exception, <strong>or</strong><br><a href="#what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu">Check the qualifying exceptions</a></li><li>Less than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-october-17-1981-and-august-1-1990-as-an-officer-eddda717-48d7-426f-a054-2fa8df160640"><h5 slot="headline">Between October 17, 1981, and August 1, 1990, as an officer</h5><div id="eddda717-48d7-426f-a054-2fa8df160640" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109710" data-analytics-faq-text="Between October 17, 1981, and August 1, 1990, as an officer"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109710"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 24 continuous months,<strong> or</strong></li><li>The full period (at least 181 days) for which you were called to active duty, <strong>or</strong></li><li>At least 181 days if you were discharged under a qualifying exception, <strong>or</strong><br><a href="#what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu">Check the qualifying exceptions</a></li><li>Less than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-may-8-1975-and-september-7-1980-post-vietnam-war-per-86b6099b-f4db-4ed0-8843-34b7bf8f701b"><h5 slot="headline">Between May 8, 1975, and September 7, 1980 (post-Vietnam War period)</h5><div id="86b6099b-f4db-4ed0-8843-34b7bf8f701b" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109711" data-analytics-faq-text="Between May 8, 1975, and September 7, 1980 (post-Vietnam War period)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109711"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>181 continuous days, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Less than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-may-8-1975-and-october-16-1981-as-an-officer-9f8e6b40-d632-47ff-9565-d869407ecfd6"><h5 slot="headline">Between May 8, 1975, and October 16, 1981, as an officer</h5><div id="9f8e6b40-d632-47ff-9565-d869407ecfd6" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109712" data-analytics-faq-text="Between May 8, 1975, and October 16, 1981, as an officer"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109712"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>181 continuous days, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Less than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-august-5-1964-and-may-7-1975-vietnam-war-e94d7137-799c-49e7-922a-c0b4a5b67c73"><h5 slot="headline">Between August 5, 1964, and May 7, 1975 (Vietnam War)</h5><div id="e94d7137-799c-49e7-922a-c0b4a5b67c73" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109713" data-analytics-faq-text="Between August 5, 1964, and May 7, 1975 (Vietnam War)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109713"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 90 total days, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Less than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-november-1-1955-and-may-7-1975-in-the-republic-of-vi-2b15d0ed-266f-41d9-806b-4baaea378f99"><h5 slot="headline">Between November 1, 1955, and May 7, 1975, in the Republic of Vietnam</h5><div id="2b15d0ed-266f-41d9-806b-4baaea378f99" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109714" data-analytics-faq-text="Between November 1, 1955, and May 7, 1975, in the Republic of Vietnam"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109714"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 90 total days,<strong> or</strong></li><li>Less than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-february-1-1955-and-august-4-1964-post-korean-war-pe-6589342f-2163-4956-9f8a-97d7a888b9cb"><h5 slot="headline">Between February 1, 1955, and August 4, 1964 (post-Korean War period)</h5><div id="6589342f-2163-4956-9f8a-97d7a888b9cb" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109715" data-analytics-faq-text="Between February 1, 1955, and August 4, 1964 (post-Korean War period)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109715"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 181 total days, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Less than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-june-27-1950-and-january-31-1955-korean-war-f9ad362b-8847-4ae3-ab38-245878ecef84"><h5 slot="headline">Between June 27, 1950, and January 31, 1955 (Korean War)</h5><div id="f9ad362b-8847-4ae3-ab38-245878ecef84" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109716" data-analytics-faq-text="Between June 27, 1950, and January 31, 1955 (Korean War)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109716"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 90 total days, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Less than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-july-26-1947-and-june-26-1950-post-wwii-period-d824d58f-fb26-4ff3-afcf-c42c798fde8d"><h5 slot="headline">Between July 26, 1947, and June 26, 1950 (post-WWII period)</h5><div id="d824d58f-fb26-4ff3-afcf-c42c798fde8d" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109717" data-analytics-faq-text="Between July 26, 1947, and June 26, 1950 (post-WWII period)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109717"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 181 continuous days,<strong> or</strong></li><li>Less than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item><va-accordion-item class="va-accordion-item" id="between-september-16-1940-and-july-25-1947-wwii-e8be4c95-038c-40fb-a4d0-98e7d21c19be"><h5 slot="headline">Between September 16, 1940, and July 25, 1947 (WWII)</h5><div id="e8be4c95-038c-40fb-a4d0-98e7d21c19be" data-template="paragraphs/collapsible_panel__panel" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--collapsible_panel_item" data-entity-id="109718" data-analytics-faq-text="Between September 16, 1940, and July 25, 1947 (WWII)"><div id="collapsible_panel_item-109718"><div itemProp="text"><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 90 total days, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Less than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability</li></ul></div></div></div></va-accordion-item></va-accordion></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h3>For National Guard members</h3><p>You meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 90 days of non-training active-duty Title 10 service, <strong>or</strong></li><li>At least 90 days of active-duty service including at least 30 consecutive days (your DD214 must show 32 USC sections 316, 502, 503, 504, or 505 activation), <strong>or</strong></li><li>6 creditable years in the National Guard, and you continue to serve, <strong>or</strong></li><li>6 creditable years in the National Guard and you were discharged honorably or placed on the retired list</li></ul></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h3>For Reserve members</h3><p>You meet the minimum length of service requirement if you served for:</p><ul><li>At least 90 days of non-training active-duty service, <strong>or</strong></li><li>6 creditable years in the Selected Reserve, and you continue to serve, <strong>or</strong></li><li>6 creditable years in the Selected Reserve and you were discharged honorably or placed on the retired list</li></ul></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a_section"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I request a COE?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>You can request a COE online right now, or you can ask your lender to submit an online application for you.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003cva-link-action href=\"https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/request-coe-form-26-1880\" text=\"Request a COE\" type=\"primary\" />\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"61f76c4d-0631-48d1-8706-bbf1354c71dc\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)\">Learn more about how to request a COE\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I don’t meet the minimum service requirements?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>You may still be able to get a COE if you were discharged under 1 of the qualifying exceptions listed here. You can apply, and we’ll review your service records to determine if you qualify for a COE.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>You must have been discharged under 1 of these exceptions:\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>Hardship, \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>The convenience of the government (you must have served at least 20 months of a 2-year enlistment), \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>Early out (you must have served 21 months of a 2-year enlistment), \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>Involuntary reduction in force, \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>Certain medical conditions, \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>A service-connected disability (a disability related to your military service)\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I do if I received an other than honorable, bad conduct, or dishonorable discharge?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>If you’ve received an other than honorable, bad conduct, or dishonorable discharge, you may not be eligible for VA benefits. You can apply, and we’ll review your service records to determine if you qualify for a COE.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>There are 2 ways you can try to qualify:\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003cp lang=\"EN-US\">Apply for a discharge upgrade\u003c/p>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cp lang=\"EN-US\">Ask for a VA Character of Discharge review\u003c/p>\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\u003cp lang=\"EN-US\">\u003ca href=\"https://www.va.gov/discharge-upgrade-instructions/introduction/\" hreflang=\"en\">Learn about applying for a discharge upgrade and requesting a Character of Discharge review\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a COE as a surviving spouse?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>You may be able to get a COE if you’re a surviving spouse and 1 of these is true for you:\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>You’re eligible for or currently receiving certain types of VA Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.), \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>You’re the spouse of an active-duty service member who’s missing in action (MIA) or being held as a prisoner of war (POW)\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"/family-and-caregiver-benefits/housing-assistance/surviving-spouse-home-loan\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"93b3819f-f40e-4cf0-89ea-5638434b8599\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Home loans for surviving spouses\">Find out how to request a COE as a surviving spouse\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a COE in any other situations?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>You may be able to get a COE if you meet at least 1 of these requirements.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>At least 1 of these must be true:\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>You’re a U.S. citizen who served in the Armed Forces of a government allied with the U.S. in World War II, \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>You served as a member in certain organizations\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>These roles in organizations can include:\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>Public Health Service officer\u003c/li>\u003cli>Cadet at the United States Military, Air Force, or Coast Guard Academy\u003c/li>\u003cli>Midshipman at the United States Naval Academy\u003c/li>\u003cli>Officer of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\u003c/li>\u003cli>Merchant seaman during World War II\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I reuse my COE?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>You may be able to restore an entitlement you used in the past to buy another home with a VA Native American Direct Loan or VA-backed loan if you meet at least 1 of these requirements and continue to meet the eligibility requirements listed on this page.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>At least 1 of these must be true:\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>You’ve sold the home you bought with the prior loan and have paid that loan in full, \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>A qualified Veteran-transferee agrees to assume your loan and substitute their entitlement for the same amount of entitlement you used originally, \u003cstrong>or\u003c/strong>\u003c/li>\u003cli>You’ve repaid your prior loan in full, but haven’t sold the home you bought with that loan (you can only do this once)\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\u003cp>You can request a COE with an entitlement restoration online. You can also ask your lender to submit an online application for you, or you can fill out a Request for a Certificate of Eligibility (VA Form 26-1880) and send it to the VA address listed on the form.\u003c/p>\u003cp>If you don't meet at least 1 of the requirements to restore the entitlement you used in the past, you may still have remaining entitlement to buy or refinance another home with a VA Native American Direct Loan or VA-backed loan.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"/forms/26-1880\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"e93e79cd-4ce5-46e0-821a-cb09ac146fa8\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"VA Form 26-1880\">Get VA Form 26-1880 to download\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I have questions about my eligibility?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\u003cp>If you have any questions about your eligibility for a VA home loan, call VA Loan Guaranty Service at \u003cva-telephone contact=\"877-827-3702\" extension=\"\">\u003c/va-telephone>&nbsp;(TTY: 711). We’re here Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. ET.\u003c/p>\u003cp>You can also submit your questions online through the Loan Guaranty support portal. You’ll need to sign in or create an account first.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"https://yourit.va.gov/csp\">Go to our Loan Guaranty support portal\u003c/a>\u003c/p>"}}]}</script><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="how-do-i-request-a-coe">How do I request a COE?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>You can request a COE online right now, or you can ask your lender to submit an online application for you.</p><p><va-link-action href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/request-coe-form-26-1880" text="Request a COE" type="primary" /></p><p><a href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="61f76c4d-0631-48d1-8706-bbf1354c71dc" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)">Learn more about how to request a COE</a></p></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu">What if I don’t meet the minimum service requirements?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>You may still be able to get a COE if you were discharged under 1 of the qualifying exceptions listed here. You can apply, and we’ll review your service records to determine if you qualify for a COE.</p><p><strong>You must have been discharged under 1 of these exceptions:</strong></p><ul><li>Hardship, <strong>or</strong></li><li>The convenience of the government (you must have served at least 20 months of a 2-year enlistment), <strong>or</strong></li><li>Early out (you must have served 21 months of a 2-year enlistment), <strong>or</strong></li><li>Involuntary reduction in force, <strong>or</strong></li><li>Certain medical conditions, <strong>or</strong></li><li>A service-connected disability (a disability related to your military service)</li></ul></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="what-should-i-do-if-i-received">What should I do if I received an other than honorable, bad conduct, or dishonorable discharge?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>If you’ve received an other than honorable, bad conduct, or dishonorable discharge, you may not be eligible for VA benefits. You can apply, and we’ll review your service records to determine if you qualify for a COE.</p><p><strong>There are 2 ways you can try to qualify:</strong></p><ul><li><p lang="EN-US">Apply for a discharge upgrade</p></li><li><p lang="EN-US">Ask for a VA Character of Discharge review</p></li></ul><p lang="EN-US"><a href="https://www.va.gov/discharge-upgrade-instructions/introduction/" hreflang="en">Learn about applying for a discharge upgrade and requesting a Character of Discharge review</a></p></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="can-i-get-a-coe-as-a-surviving">Can I get a COE as a surviving spouse?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>You may be able to get a COE if you’re a surviving spouse and 1 of these is true for you:</p><ul><li>You’re eligible for or currently receiving certain types of VA Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.), <strong>or</strong></li><li>You’re the spouse of an active-duty service member who’s missing in action (MIA) or being held as a prisoner of war (POW)</li></ul><p><a href="/family-and-caregiver-benefits/housing-assistance/surviving-spouse-home-loan" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="93b3819f-f40e-4cf0-89ea-5638434b8599" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Home loans for surviving spouses">Find out how to request a COE as a surviving spouse</a></p></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="can-i-get-a-coe-in-any-other-s">Can I get a COE in any other situations?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>You may be able to get a COE if you meet at least 1 of these requirements.</p><p><strong>At least 1 of these must be true:</strong></p><ul><li>You’re a U.S. citizen who served in the Armed Forces of a government allied with the U.S. in World War II, <strong>or</strong></li><li>You served as a member in certain organizations</li></ul><p><strong>These roles in organizations can include:</strong></p><ul><li>Public Health Service officer</li><li>Cadet at the United States Military, Air Force, or Coast Guard Academy</li><li>Midshipman at the United States Naval Academy</li><li>Officer of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration</li><li>Merchant seaman during World War II</li></ul></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="can-i-reuse-my-coe">Can I reuse my COE?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>You may be able to restore an entitlement you used in the past to buy another home with a VA Native American Direct Loan or VA-backed loan if you meet at least 1 of these requirements and continue to meet the eligibility requirements listed on this page.</p><p><strong>At least 1 of these must be true:</strong></p><ul><li>You’ve sold the home you bought with the prior loan and have paid that loan in full, <strong>or</strong></li><li>A qualified Veteran-transferee agrees to assume your loan and substitute their entitlement for the same amount of entitlement you used originally, <strong>or</strong></li><li>You’ve repaid your prior loan in full, but haven’t sold the home you bought with that loan (you can only do this once)</li></ul><p>You can request a COE with an entitlement restoration online. You can also ask your lender to submit an online application for you, or you can fill out a Request for a Certificate of Eligibility (VA Form 26-1880) and send it to the VA address listed on the form.</p><p>If you don't meet at least 1 of the requirements to restore the entitlement you used in the past, you may still have remaining entitlement to buy or refinance another home with a VA Native American Direct Loan or VA-backed loan.</p><p><a href="/forms/26-1880" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="e93e79cd-4ce5-46e0-821a-cb09ac146fa8" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="VA Form 26-1880">Get VA Form 26-1880 to download</a></p></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/q_a"><div class="vads-u-display--flex"><h2 id="what-if-i-have-questions-about">What if I have questions about my eligibility?</h2></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><p>If you have any questions about your eligibility for a VA home loan, call VA Loan Guaranty Service at <va-telephone contact="877-827-3702" extension=""></va-telephone>&nbsp;(TTY: 711). We’re here Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. ET.</p><p>You can also submit your questions online through the Loan Guaranty support portal. You’ll need to sign in or create an account first.</p><p><a href="https://yourit.va.gov/csp">Go to our Loan Guaranty support portal</a></p></div></div></div></div><div data-template="paragraphs/wysiwyg" data-paragraph-type="paragraph--wysiwyg"><div itemProp="text"><h2 id="get-more-information-432">Get more information</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.benefits.va.gov/homeloans/index.asp">Learn more about VA home loan guaranty benefits</a></li><li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vYr5QVwL1Ow&amp;list=PLA93A5833057D78B7&amp;index=7">Play a video about the costs of home ownership (YouTube)</a></li><li><a href="https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/201503_cfpb_your-home-loan-toolkit-web.pdf">Check out the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau’s home loan toolkit (PDF)</a></li></ul></div></div><div class="va-nav-linkslist va-nav-linkslist--related"><section data-template="paragraphs/list_of_link_teasers" data-entity-id="310599b8-f86b-4e60-b792-d72a053727b2"><h2 id="loan-options" class="vads-u-border-bottom--1px vads-u-border-color--base-light vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-padding-top--2 vads-u-padding-bottom--0p5">Loan options</h2><ul class="usa-unstyled-list"><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="72e26f74-169b-4845-bf8e-bbcc6c8e7ff7" data-links-list-header="Purchase loan" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/" target="" text="Purchase loan"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Looking to buy a home? Find out if you can get a VA-backed purchase loan and get better terms than with a private lender loan.</p></li><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="54763df7-1070-4f4c-a0d8-ec1e17e012d8" data-links-list-header="Interest Rate Reduction Refinance Loan (IRRRL)" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/interest-rate-reduction-loan/" target="" text="Interest Rate Reduction Refinance Loan (IRRRL)"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Have an existing VA home loan? Find out if you can get a VA-backed IRRRL to help reduce your monthly payments or make them more stable.</p></li><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="bbca02dd-0937-41f1-b733-c01aa3f68d7f" data-links-list-header="Cash-out refinance loan" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/cash-out-loan/" target="" text="Cash-out refinance loan"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Want to take cash out of your home equity to pay off debt, pay for school, or take care of other needs? Find out if you can get a VA-backed cash-out refinance loan.</p></li><li class="vads-u-margin-y--2" data-template="paragraphs/linkTeaser" data-entity-id="292693a7-925d-4c5a-8594-9904c2aadb90" data-links-list-header="Native American Direct Loan (NADL) program" data-links-list-section-header="Loan options"><p class="vads-u-margin--0 vads-u-font-weight--bold"><va-link href="/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/native-american-direct-loan/" target="" text="Native American Direct Loan (NADL) program"></va-link></p><p class="vads-u-margin--0">Are you a Native American Veteran or a Veteran married to a Native American? Find out if you can get a loan through our NADL program to buy, build, or improve a home on federal trust land.</p></li></ul></section></div><va-back-to-top></va-back-to-top><div data-testid="content-footer" class="last-updated "><div class="mobile-lg:vads-u-display--flex above-footer-elements-container"><div class="vads-u-flex--auto"><span class="vads-u-text-align--justify"><p>Last updated: <time dateTime="2026-09-22">September 22, 2026</time></p></span></div><div class="vads-u-flex--1 vads-u-text-align--right"><va-button id="mdFormButton" disable-analytics="" secondary="" class="vads-u-background-color--white" text="Feedback"></va-button></div></div></div></article></div></div></div></div></div></main><footer class="footer"><div id="footerNav" data-testid="footer" data-minimal-footer="false"></div></footer><div id="logout-modal-root"></div></div><script id="__NEXT_DATA__" type="application/json" nonce="3kkSV8HoX0zX839iRarOrVH1hGuXnnl8">{"props":{"pageProps":{"previewTokenError":false,"preview":false,"serializedResource":{"data":{"id":"93a096d5-1c1a-4248-bad0-816a22fd13c3","entityId":753,"entityPath":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility","type":"node--page","published":true,"moderationState":"published","title":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs","metatags":[{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"title","content":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs | Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"description","content":"Learn about VA home loan eligibility requirements for a VA direct loan (Native American Direct Loan) or a VA-backed loan. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify based on your service history and duty status. To get financing for a VA-backed home loan, you must meet credit, income, and occupancy requirements from both us and your lender."}},{"tag":"link","attributes":{"rel":"image_src","href":"https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:site_name","content":"Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:title","content":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs | Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:description","content":"Learn about VA home loan eligibility requirements for a VA direct loan (Native American Direct Loan) or a VA-backed loan. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify based on your service history and duty status. To get financing for a VA-backed home loan, you must meet credit, income, and occupancy requirements from both us and your lender."}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:image","content":"https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:image:alt","content":"U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:card","content":"summary_large_image"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:site","content":"@DeptVetAffairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:description","content":"Learn about VA home loan eligibility requirements. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify for a VA-backed loan based on your service history and duty status."}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:title","content":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs | Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:image:alt","content":"U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:image","content":"https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png"}}],"breadcrumbs":[{"href":"/","label":"Home"},{"href":"/housing-assistance","label":"Housing assistance"},{"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans","label":"VA-backed home loans"},{"href":"","label":"Eligibility for VA home loan programs"}],"lastUpdated":"2026-09-22T18:48:05+00:00","description":"Learn about VA home loan eligibility requirements. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify for a VA-backed loan based on your service history and duty status.","introText":"\u003cp\u003eLearn about VA home loan eligibility requirements for a VA direct loan (Native American Direct Loan) or a VA-backed loan. Find out how to request a Certificate of Eligibility (COE) to show your lender that you qualify based on your service history and duty status. To get financing for a VA-backed home loan, you must meet credit, income, and occupancy requirements from both us and your lender.\u003c/p\u003e\n","showTableOfContents":false,"alert":null,"featuredContent":[{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"Can I get a COE for a Native American Direct Loan or a VA-backed home loan?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"a33e27bf-0856-4165-9833-a1a338baa65e","html":"\u003cp\u003eYou may be able to get a COE if you meet the minimum active-duty service requirements for your service period or were discharged under a qualifying exception.\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"96a84744-a25f-420b-ba2d-aa54325b0db0"}],"mainContent":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"cc41acb0-f850-4080-9555-6cf1395620ad","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"minimum-active-duty-service-re\"\u003eMinimum active-duty service requirements\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3\u003eFor service members\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you’ve served for at least 90 continuous days (all at once, without a break in service), you meet the minimum active-duty service requirement.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eFor Veterans\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe minimum active-duty service requirements depend on when you served.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWhen did you serve?\u003c/h4\u003e"},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel","id":"b87aa60f-7bcc-4b02-b534-1099d5b61a32","entityId":109719,"paragraphs":[{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"14386229-a09d-4979-82e4-40718e5670d7","entityId":109708,"title":"Between August 2, 1990, and the present (Gulf War period to present)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 24 continuous months,\u003cstrong\u003e or\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe full period (at least 90 days) for which you were called or ordered to active duty, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 days if you were discharged under a qualifying exception, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ca href=\"#what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu\"\u003eCheck the qualifying exceptions\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"a554099d-a035-4291-b988-5d0b96545fbc","entityId":109709,"title":" Between September 8, 1980, and August 1, 1990","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 24 continuous months, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe full period (at least 181 days) for which you were called to active duty, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 181 days if you were discharged under a qualifying exception, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ca href=\"#what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu\"\u003eCheck the qualifying exceptions\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"eddda717-48d7-426f-a054-2fa8df160640","entityId":109710,"title":"Between October 17, 1981, and August 1, 1990, as an officer","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 24 continuous months,\u003cstrong\u003e or\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe full period (at least 181 days) for which you were called to active duty, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 181 days if you were discharged under a qualifying exception, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ca href=\"#what-if-i-dont-meet-the-minimu\"\u003eCheck the qualifying exceptions\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"86b6099b-f4db-4ed0-8843-34b7bf8f701b","entityId":109711,"title":"Between May 8, 1975, and September 7, 1980 (post-Vietnam War period)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e181 continuous days, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"9f8e6b40-d632-47ff-9565-d869407ecfd6","entityId":109712,"title":"Between May 8, 1975, and October 16, 1981, as an officer","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e181 continuous days, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"e94d7137-799c-49e7-922a-c0b4a5b67c73","entityId":109713,"title":"Between August 5, 1964, and May 7, 1975 (Vietnam War)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 total days, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"2b15d0ed-266f-41d9-806b-4baaea378f99","entityId":109714,"title":"Between November 1, 1955, and May 7, 1975, in the Republic of Vietnam","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 total days,\u003cstrong\u003e or\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"6589342f-2163-4956-9f8a-97d7a888b9cb","entityId":109715,"title":"Between February 1, 1955, and August 4, 1964 (post-Korean War period)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 181 total days, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"f9ad362b-8847-4ae3-ab38-245878ecef84","entityId":109716,"title":"Between June 27, 1950, and January 31, 1955 (Korean War)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 total days, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"d824d58f-fb26-4ff3-afcf-c42c798fde8d","entityId":109717,"title":"Between July 26, 1947, and June 26, 1950 (post-WWII period)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 181 continuous days,\u003cstrong\u003e or\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 181 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]},{"type":"paragraph--collapsible_panel_item","id":"e8be4c95-038c-40fb-a4d0-98e7d21c19be","entityId":109718,"title":"Between September 16, 1940, and July 25, 1947 (WWII)","wysiwyg":"\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 total days, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLess than 90 days if you were discharged for a service-connected disability\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","paragraphs":[]}],"bordered":false},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"2bc82708-6acf-4697-ab3a-facd011c58ec","html":"\u003ch3\u003eFor National Guard members\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum active-duty service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 days of non-training active-duty Title 10 service, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 days of active-duty service including at least 30 consecutive days (your DD214 must show 32 USC sections 316, 502, 503, 504, or 505 activation), \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e6 creditable years in the National Guard, and you continue to serve, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e6 creditable years in the National Guard and you were discharged honorably or placed on the retired list\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e"},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"4df40570-ab88-42ce-b7f4-ac0e658cdabf","html":"\u003ch3\u003eFor Reserve members\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou meet the minimum length of service requirement if you served for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAt least 90 days of non-training active-duty service, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e6 creditable years in the Selected Reserve, and you continue to serve, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e6 creditable years in the Selected Reserve and you were discharged honorably or placed on the retired list\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e"},{"header":null,"intro":null,"questions":[{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"How do I request a COE?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"944e2c7b-37c6-4275-86f1-614f21d56d4e","html":"\u003cp\u003eYou can request a COE online right now, or you can ask your lender to submit an online application for you.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cva-link-action href=\"https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/request-coe-form-26-1880\" text=\"Request a COE\" type=\"primary\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/housing-assistance/home-loans/how-to-request-coe\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"61f76c4d-0631-48d1-8706-bbf1354c71dc\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"How to request a VA home loan Certificate of Eligibility (COE)\"\u003eLearn more about how to request a COE\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"8a7849b0-1f90-41ad-8a4b-462db4de6f7c"},{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"What if I don’t meet the minimum service requirements?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"b032dc01-c590-42d3-8500-973eb46fd27f","html":"\u003cp\u003eYou may still be able to get a COE if you were discharged under 1 of the qualifying exceptions listed here. You can apply, and we’ll review your service records to determine if you qualify for a COE.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou must have been discharged under 1 of these exceptions:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eHardship, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe convenience of the government (you must have served at least 20 months of a 2-year enlistment), \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eEarly out (you must have served 21 months of a 2-year enlistment), \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eInvoluntary reduction in force, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCertain medical conditions, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eA service-connected disability (a disability related to your military service)\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e"}],"id":"89bc40a7-05db-4aa9-bfd3-94dd435a3608"},{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"What should I do if I received an other than honorable, bad conduct, or dishonorable discharge?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"79545757-288c-4665-ad58-74ecbfa34ac9","html":"\u003cp\u003eIf you’ve received an other than honorable, bad conduct, or dishonorable discharge, you may not be eligible for VA benefits. You can apply, and we’ll review your service records to determine if you qualify for a COE.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThere are 2 ways you can try to qualify:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp lang=\"EN-US\"\u003eApply for a discharge upgrade\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp lang=\"EN-US\"\u003eAsk for a VA Character of Discharge review\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp lang=\"EN-US\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.va.gov/discharge-upgrade-instructions/introduction/\" hreflang=\"en\"\u003eLearn about applying for a discharge upgrade and requesting a Character of Discharge review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"74724242-5526-4874-9652-cbfadb12dbe6"},{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"Can I get a COE as a surviving spouse?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"3652a701-ff38-48e7-bf84-7d2236d6dfc4","html":"\u003cp\u003eYou may be able to get a COE if you’re a surviving spouse and 1 of these is true for you:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou’re eligible for or currently receiving certain types of VA Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.), \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou’re the spouse of an active-duty service member who’s missing in action (MIA) or being held as a prisoner of war (POW)\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/family-and-caregiver-benefits/housing-assistance/surviving-spouse-home-loan\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"93b3819f-f40e-4cf0-89ea-5638434b8599\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"Home loans for surviving spouses\"\u003eFind out how to request a COE as a surviving spouse\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"7a03c64b-1b65-479c-84d7-4332e56de787"},{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"Can I get a COE in any other situations?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"6ab68147-2616-4718-a98c-7bb025698e14","html":"\u003cp\u003eYou may be able to get a COE if you meet at least 1 of these requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAt least 1 of these must be true:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou’re a U.S. citizen who served in the Armed Forces of a government allied with the U.S. in World War II, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou served as a member in certain organizations\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThese roles in organizations can include:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ePublic Health Service officer\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCadet at the United States Military, Air Force, or Coast Guard Academy\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eMidshipman at the United States Naval Academy\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOfficer of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eMerchant seaman during World War II\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e"}],"id":"f9f51081-3073-4525-9787-ed89fde7fceb"},{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"Can I reuse my COE?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"4428694e-1fed-4fc0-abdf-d063126b4f73","html":"\u003cp\u003eYou may be able to restore an entitlement you used in the past to buy another home with a VA Native American Direct Loan or VA-backed loan if you meet at least 1 of these requirements and continue to meet the eligibility requirements listed on this page.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAt least 1 of these must be true:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou’ve sold the home you bought with the prior loan and have paid that loan in full, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eA qualified Veteran-transferee agrees to assume your loan and substitute their entitlement for the same amount of entitlement you used originally, \u003cstrong\u003eor\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou’ve repaid your prior loan in full, but haven’t sold the home you bought with that loan (you can only do this once)\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou can request a COE with an entitlement restoration online. You can also ask your lender to submit an online application for you, or you can fill out a Request for a Certificate of Eligibility (VA Form 26-1880) and send it to the VA address listed on the form.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you don't meet at least 1 of the requirements to restore the entitlement you used in the past, you may still have remaining entitlement to buy or refinance another home with a VA Native American Direct Loan or VA-backed loan.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/forms/26-1880\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"e93e79cd-4ce5-46e0-821a-cb09ac146fa8\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" title=\"VA Form 26-1880\"\u003eGet VA Form 26-1880 to download\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"7f4da4d1-f99c-4604-bc60-d1454fac0941"},{"type":"paragraph--q_a","question":"What if I have questions about my eligibility?","answers":[{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"f13ae811-ec5d-42e4-8ec8-375214f6a98f","html":"\u003cp\u003eIf you have any questions about your eligibility for a VA home loan, call VA Loan Guaranty Service at \u003cva-telephone contact=\"877-827-3702\" extension=\"\"\u003e\u003c/va-telephone\u003e\u0026nbsp;(TTY: 711). We’re here Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. ET.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou can also submit your questions online through the Loan Guaranty support portal. You’ll need to sign in or create an account first.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://yourit.va.gov/csp\"\u003eGo to our Loan Guaranty support portal\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"id":"e2d31969-fbc1-4476-97f6-2f36e9cb92a5"}],"displayAccordion":false,"type":"paragraph--q_a_section","id":"d57c648a-d645-44ed-a0e0-0852da92003c"},{"type":"paragraph--wysiwyg","id":"149c9201-a6c6-4480-acc6-810d7e6a138c","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"get-more-information-432\"\u003eGet more information\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.benefits.va.gov/homeloans/index.asp\"\u003eLearn more about VA home loan guaranty benefits\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vYr5QVwL1Ow\u0026amp;list=PLA93A5833057D78B7\u0026amp;index=7\"\u003ePlay a video about the costs of home ownership (YouTube)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/201503_cfpb_your-home-loan-toolkit-web.pdf\"\u003eCheck out the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau’s home loan toolkit (PDF)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e"}],"relatedLinks":{"type":"paragraph--list_of_link_teasers","id":"310599b8-f86b-4e60-b792-d72a053727b2","entityId":4954,"title":"Loan options","linkTeasers":[{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"72e26f74-169b-4845-bf8e-bbcc6c8e7ff7","entityId":4955,"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/","label":"Purchase loan","summary":"Looking to buy a home? Find out if you can get a VA-backed purchase loan and get better terms than with a private lender loan."},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"54763df7-1070-4f4c-a0d8-ec1e17e012d8","entityId":4957,"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/interest-rate-reduction-loan/","label":"Interest Rate Reduction Refinance Loan (IRRRL)","summary":"Have an existing VA home loan? Find out if you can get a VA-backed IRRRL to help reduce your monthly payments or make them more stable."},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"bbca02dd-0937-41f1-b733-c01aa3f68d7f","entityId":4958,"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/cash-out-loan/","label":"Cash-out refinance loan","summary":"Want to take cash out of your home equity to pay off debt, pay for school, or take care of other needs? Find out if you can get a VA-backed cash-out refinance loan."},{"type":"paragraph--link_teaser","id":"292693a7-925d-4c5a-8594-9904c2aadb90","entityId":4956,"href":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/native-american-direct-loan/","label":"Native American Direct Loan (NADL) program","summary":"Are you a Native American Veteran or a Veteran married to a Native American? Find out if you can get a loan through our NADL program to buy, build, or improve a home on federal trust land."}]},"administration":{"entityId":68,"name":"Housing assistance benefits hub"},"menu":{"rootPath":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility/","data":{"name":"Housing assistance","description":null,"links":[{"description":null,"expanded":false,"label":"Housing assistance","links":[{"description":null,"expanded":true,"label":"VA home loans","links":[{"description":null,"expanded":true,"label":"VA-backed home loans","links":[{"description":null,"expanded":true,"label":"Loan types","links":[{"description":null,"expanded":false,"label":"Purchase loan","links":[],"url":{"path":"/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan"},"lovellSection":null},{"description":null,"expanded":true,"label":"Native American Direct Loan","links":[{"description":null,"expanded":false,"la